=head1 NAME

Strada::JIT - Runtime eval() for Strada

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    use lib "lib";
    use Strada::JIT;

    # Initialize with auto-detected compiler (tcc preferred, gcc fallback)
    Strada::JIT::init();

    # Or specify compiler explicitly
    Strada::JIT::init("gcc");

    # Evaluate expressions - returns the result
    my scalar $result = Strada::JIT::eval("1 + 2");             # returns 3
    my scalar $s = Strada::JIT::eval("\"hello\" . \" world\""); # returns "hello world"

    # Variables persist across eval calls
    Strada::JIT::eval("my int \$x = 42;");
    my scalar $val = Strada::JIT::eval("\$x * 2");   # returns 84

    # Function definitions persist
    Strada::JIT::eval("func twice(int \$n) int { return \$n * 2; }");
    my scalar $r = Strada::JIT::eval("twice(21)");   # returns 42

    # Void calls (say, print, etc.) return undef
    Strada::JIT::eval("say(\"hello from eval\");");

    # Error handling - compilation/runtime errors throw exceptions
    try {
        Strada::JIT::eval("this is not valid code");
    } catch ($e) {
        say("Eval error: " . $e);
    }

    # Get/set variables directly
    Strada::JIT::set("x", 100);
    my scalar $v = Strada::JIT::get("x");   # returns 100

    # Add library search paths
    Strada::JIT::add_lib_path("/path/to/libs");

    # Reset all state
    Strada::JIT::reset();

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Strada::JIT provides runtime code evaluation for Strada programs, similar to
Perl's C<eval STRING>. It compiles Strada code to C via stradac, then
to a shared library via tcc or gcc, loads it with dlopen, and executes
it. Variables and function definitions persist across eval calls via a
shared state hash.

This enables programs to compile and execute Strada code at runtime for
use cases like plugin systems, configuration evaluation, scripting
engines, and interactive tools.

=head1 FUNCTIONS

=head2 Strada::JIT::init(str ...@args)

Initialize the JIT engine. Must be called before C<eval()>.

Auto-detects the stradac compiler, runtime path, and C compiler. Prefers
tcc for faster compilation, falls back to gcc.

Pass an optional compiler name to override auto-detection:

    Strada::JIT::init();        # auto-detect
    Strada::JIT::init("tcc");   # force tcc
    Strada::JIT::init("gcc");   # force gcc

Throws an exception if stradac or a C compiler cannot be found.

=head2 Strada::JIT::eval(str $code) scalar

Evaluate Strada code and return the result.

Expressions return their value. For multi-statement code, the value is the
LAST expression (Perl-ish C<eval> semantics) — e.g.
C<eval("my %h=(); $h{'a'}=41; $h{'a'}+1")> returns 42. Code whose final
top-level statement ends in C<;>, or a trailing void call (C<say>, C<print>,
etc.), returns undef.

Variables declared with C<my> persist across eval calls. Function
definitions (C<func ...>) are accumulated and available in subsequent
evals. Import statements (C<use>, C<import_lib>) are registered and
included in all subsequent evals. Package declarations set the current
package context.

Throws an exception on compilation or runtime errors.

=head2 Strada::JIT::get(str $name) scalar

Get a variable value from the persistent state hash. Returns undef if
the variable does not exist.

    Strada::JIT::eval("my int \$x = 42;");
    my scalar $v = Strada::JIT::get("x");   # 42

=head2 Strada::JIT::set(str $name, scalar $value)

Set a variable value in the persistent state hash. Also registers the
variable type as C<scalar> if not already known.

    Strada::JIT::set("count", 0);

=head2 Strada::JIT::add_lib_path(str $path)

Add a library search path for stradac (equivalent to C<-L> flag).
Duplicate paths are ignored.

    Strada::JIT::add_lib_path("lib");
    Strada::JIT::add_lib_path("/usr/local/lib/strada");

=head2 Strada::JIT::reset()

Clear all persistent state: variables, function definitions, imports,
package name, and the eval counter.

=head2 Strada::JIT::debug(int $enabled)

Enable (1) or disable (0) debug mode. When enabled, the generated Strada
source for each eval is printed to stdout.

=head2 Strada::JIT::compiler() str

Returns the name of the detected C compiler ("tcc" or "gcc").

=head1 ARCHITECTURE

Each C<Strada::JIT::eval()> call performs these steps:

=over

=item 1. Scan code for variable declarations, function definitions, imports

=item 2. Generate a complete Strada source file wrapping the code

=item 3. Compile with stradac to C

=item 4. Compile with tcc/gcc to a shared library (.so)

=item 5. Load with dlopen, find the entry function with dlsym

=item 6. Call the function via core::dl_call_sv, passing the state hash

=item 7. Clean up temp files

=back

The generated source restores persisted variables from the state hash at
the start of the function and exports them back at the end.

=head1 LIMITATIONS

=over

=item * Variables persist via save/restore through the global registry.
All variable types (scalars, arrays, hashes) use real C<my> declarations
with C<__C__> blocks to save and restore values between eval calls.
This means C<$i++>, C<s///>, and C<for (my int $i ...)> all work correctly.

=item * C<const> and C<enum> declarations require the gcc backend (tcc does
not run C<__attribute__((constructor))> for dlopen'd shared libraries).

=item * C<try/catch> requires the gcc backend (tcc lacks setjmp support).

=item * C<fn> is supported as an alias for C<func> in function definitions.

=item * Each eval invocation compiles and links a new shared library, so
there is overhead per call. Use tcc for faster compilation of simple code.

=item * The C<libtcc> in-process backend is not supported (only the
external tcc and gcc compilers).

=back

=head1 SEE ALSO

C<tools/strada-jit.strada> - Interactive REPL that uses the same
compile-load-execute approach.

=cut

package Strada::JIT;

__C__ {
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>

static int repl_command_exists(const char *cmd) {
    char path[256];
    snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "which %s >/dev/null 2>&1", cmd);
    return system(path) == 0;
}
}

# Internal state
my hash %g_var_types = ();
my array @g_functions = ();
my array @g_imports = ();
my array @g_lib_paths = ();
my str $g_stradac_path = "";
my str $g_runtime_path = "";
my str $g_compiler = "";
my int $g_eval_count = 0;
my str $g_tmpdir = "/tmp";
my int $g_tmpdir_owned = 0;
my int $g_initialized = 0;
my str $g_current_package = "";
my int $g_debug = 0;
my int $g_cdebug = 0;
my array @g_open_libs = ();
my array @g_retired_libs = ();
my array @g_our_decls = ();
my hash %g_our_decl_idx = ();
my hash %g_prev_var_types = ();
my array @g_so_files = ();
my array @g_constants = ();
my hash %g_constant_idx = ();
my hash %g_oop_packages = ();
my hash %g_ever_oop_packages = ();
my int $g_did_oop_reset = 0;
my int $g_strip_unclosed = 0;
my array @g_last_heredoc_ranges = ();

# Tracked session variables are keyed by sigil + name ("$x", "@x", "%x"), so
# `my @x` and a later `my $x` are two variables (Perl).
private func jit_vk(str $type, str $name) str {
    if ($type eq "array") { return "@" . $name; }
    if ($type eq "hash") { return "%" . $name; }
    return "$" . $name;
}
private func jit_vk_name(str $k) str { return substr($k, 1, length($k) - 1); }
private func jit_vk_sigil(str $k) str { return substr($k, 0, 1); }
# Global-registry key holding a tracked variable between evals: scalars keep
# the historical "repl::NAME"; arrays / hashes are sigil-qualified.
private func jit_vk_reg(str $k) str {
    my str $sg = jit_vk_sigil($k);
    if ($sg eq "$") { return "repl::" . jit_vk_name($k); }
    return "repl::" . $sg . jit_vk_name($k);
}
# Tracked keys in declaration order: by name, then $ @ %.
private func jit_vk_ordered() array {
    my array @tmp = ();
    foreach my str $k (keys(%g_var_types)) {
        my str $sg = jit_vk_sigil($k);
        my str $rank = "0";
        if ($sg eq "@") { $rank = "1"; }
        if ($sg eq "%") { $rank = "2"; }
        push(@tmp, jit_vk_name($k) . "\x01" . $rank . "\x01" . $k);
    }
    my array @sorted = sort { $a cmp $b } @tmp;
    my array @out = ();
    foreach my str $e (@sorted) {
        my array @parts = split("\x01", $e);
        push(@out, $parts[2]);
    }
    return @out;
}
# The C name the compiler gives a tracked variable: the first declaration of
# a name in repl_eval keeps the plain name; another sigil of the same name
# gets NAME__sga / __sgh / __sgs (Semantic, same-name-different-sigil).
private func jit_vk_cname(str $k, scalar $first_seen) str {
    my str $nm = jit_vk_name($k);
    my str $first = "" . $first_seen->{$nm};
    if (length($first) == 0 || $first eq $k) { return jit_escape_c_keyword($nm); }
    my str $sg = jit_vk_sigil($k);
    my str $tag = "s";
    if ($sg eq "@") { $tag = "a"; }
    if ($sg eq "%") { $tag = "h"; }
    return $nm . "__sg" . $tag;
}
# Public names for var_types()/state(): bare when a name has one sigil,
# sigil-qualified when several share it.
private func jit_vk_public(str $k) str {
    my str $nm = jit_vk_name($k);
    my int $n = 0;
    foreach my str $o (keys(%g_var_types)) {
        if (jit_vk_name($o) eq $nm) { $n = $n + 1; }
    }
    if ($n > 1) { return $k; }
    return $nm;
}
# A name given to get()/set(): "$x" / "@x" / "%x", or bare "x" (the scalar,
# else the only variable of that name)
private func jit_vk_lookup(str $name) str {
    my str $c0 = substr($name, 0, 1);
    if ($c0 eq "$" || $c0 eq "@" || $c0 eq "%") { return $name; }
    if (exists($g_var_types{"$" . $name})) { return "$" . $name; }
    if (exists($g_var_types{"@" . $name})) { return "@" . $name; }
    if (exists($g_var_types{"%" . $name})) { return "%" . $name; }
    return "$" . $name;
}

private func jit_escape_c_keyword(str $name) str {
    if ($name eq "for" || $name eq "while" || $name eq "if" || $name eq "else" ||
        $name eq "switch" || $name eq "case" || $name eq "default" || $name eq "break" ||
        $name eq "continue" || $name eq "return" || $name eq "goto" || $name eq "do" ||
        $name eq "int" || $name eq "char" || $name eq "float" || $name eq "double" ||
        $name eq "void" || $name eq "long" || $name eq "short" || $name eq "unsigned" ||
        $name eq "signed" || $name eq "const" || $name eq "static" || $name eq "extern" ||
        $name eq "register" || $name eq "volatile" || $name eq "auto" ||
        $name eq "struct" || $name eq "union" || $name eq "enum" || $name eq "typedef" ||
        $name eq "sizeof" || $name eq "inline" || $name eq "restrict" ||
        $name eq "alignas" || $name eq "alignof" || $name eq "constexpr" || $name eq "nullptr" ||
        $name eq "static_assert" || $name eq "thread_local" || $name eq "typeof_unqual" ||
        $name eq "STDIN" || $name eq "STDOUT" || $name eq "STDERR" ||
        $name eq "bool" || $name eq "true" || $name eq "false" || $name eq "errno" ||
        $name eq "NULL" || $name eq "EOF" || $name eq "asm" || $name eq "typeof" ||
        $name eq "pow" || $name eq "sin" || $name eq "cos" || $name eq "tan" ||
        $name eq "sqrt" || $name eq "log" || $name eq "exp" || $name eq "floor" ||
        $name eq "ceil" || $name eq "fabs" || $name eq "fmod" ||
        $name eq "free" || $name eq "malloc" || $name eq "calloc" || $name eq "realloc" ||
        $name eq "memcpy" || $name eq "memset" || $name eq "strlen" || $name eq "strcmp" ||
        $name eq "stdin" || $name eq "stdout" || $name eq "stderr") {
        return "v_" . $name;
    }
    if ($name eq "_Bool" || $name eq "_Complex" || $name eq "_Imaginary" ||
        $name eq "_Alignas" || $name eq "_Alignof" || $name eq "_Atomic" ||
        $name eq "_Generic" || $name eq "_Noreturn" || $name eq "_Static_assert" ||
        $name eq "_Thread_local") {
        return "v" . $name;
    }
    return $name;
}

# Detect stradac path
private func detect_stradac() str {
    my int $exists = 0;

    if (core::is_file("./stradac") == 1) {
        return "./stradac";
    }

    __C__ {
        exists = strada_new_int(repl_command_exists("stradac"));
    }
    if ($exists == 1) {
        return "stradac";
    }

    if (core::is_file("/usr/local/bin/stradac") == 1) {
        return "/usr/local/bin/stradac";
    }
    if (core::is_file("/usr/bin/stradac") == 1) {
        return "/usr/bin/stradac";
    }

    return "";
}

# Detect runtime path
private func detect_runtime() str {
    if (core::is_file("./runtime/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
        return "./runtime";
    }

    # The compiler found on PATH: use the runtime that belongs to it (a
    # source tree keeps it next to stradac, an installation under
    # ../lib/strada). Pairing it with another installation's headers breaks
    # as soon as the compiler emits a call the older header lacks.
    if ($g_stradac_path eq "stradac") {
        my array @path_dirs = split(":", "" . core::getenv("PATH"));
        foreach my str $path_dir (@path_dirs) {
            if (length($path_dir) == 0) { next; }
            if (core::is_file($path_dir . "/stradac") != 1) { next; }
            if (core::is_file($path_dir . "/runtime/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
                return $path_dir . "/runtime";
            }
            if (core::is_file($path_dir . "/../lib/strada/runtime/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
                return $path_dir . "/../lib/strada/runtime";
            }
            last;
        }
    }

    if ($g_stradac_path ne "" && $g_stradac_path ne "stradac") {
        my str $stradac_dir = core::dirname($g_stradac_path);
        my str $relative_runtime = $stradac_dir . "/../lib/strada/runtime";
        if (core::is_file($relative_runtime . "/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
            return $relative_runtime;
        }
    }

    if (core::is_file("/usr/local/lib/strada/runtime/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
        return "/usr/local/lib/strada/runtime";
    }
    if (core::is_file("/usr/lib/strada/runtime/strada_runtime_tcc.h") == 1) {
        return "/usr/lib/strada/runtime";
    }

    return "";
}

# Detect available C compiler. Prefers gcc — tcc is faster but has
# known correctness gaps (see project_perla_tcc_dclone_bug in memory):
# tcc-compiled output can silently misbehave on edge cases that gcc
# handles correctly. With strada's -O0 speed flags, gcc is fast enough
# for JIT use without giving up correctness.
private func detect_compiler() str {
    my int $has_tcc = 0;
    my int $has_gcc = 0;

    __C__ {
        has_tcc = strada_new_int(repl_command_exists("tcc"));
        has_gcc = strada_new_int(repl_command_exists("gcc"));
    }

    if ($has_gcc == 1) {
        return "gcc";
    }
    if ($has_tcc == 1) {
        return "tcc";
    }
    return "";
}

# Single-quote a string safely for /bin/sh
private func shell_quote(str $s) str {
    my str $out = "'";
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $len = length($s);
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $ch = substr($s, $i, 1);
        if ($ch eq "'") {
            $out = $out . "'\\''";
        } else {
            $out = $out . $ch;
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return $out . "'";
}

# Check if input looks like a function definition
private func get_target_package() str {
    if ($g_current_package ne "" && $g_current_package ne "main") {
        return $g_current_package;
    }
    return "repl";
}

private func track_oop_package(str $pkg) void {
    if ($pkg ne "" && $pkg ne "main") {
        $g_oop_packages{$pkg} = 1;
        $g_ever_oop_packages{$pkg} = 1;
    }
}

# Check if input is a function definition
private func is_function_def(str $input) int {
    # Accepts both parens form `func name(...)` and no-parens form `func name { ... }`
    # (or `func name rettype { ... }`).
    if ($input =~ /^\s*(private\s+|async\s+)*(func|fn)\s+\w+\s*(\(|(\w+\s+)?\{)/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Check if input is a method modifier (before/after/around)
private func is_modifier_def(str $input) int {
    if ($input =~ /^\s*(before|after|around)\s+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Extract function name from a function definition (including optional package prefix)
private func get_function_name(str $func_def) str {
    my str $s = $func_def;
    $s =~ s/^\s*//;
    my str $pkg = "";
    if ($s =~ /^package\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*)\s*;/) {
        $pkg = $s;
        $pkg =~ s/^package\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*)\s*;[\s\S]*$/$1/;
        $s =~ s/^package\s+[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*\s*;\s*//;
    }
    $s =~ s/^(private\s+|async\s+)+//;
    if (!($s =~ /^(func|fn)\s+/)) {
        return "";
    }
    $s =~ s/^(func|fn)\s+//;
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $len = length($s);
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $ch = substr($s, $i, 1);
        if ($ch eq "(" || $ch eq "{" || $ch eq " " || $ch eq "\t" || $ch eq "\n" || $ch eq "\r") {
            last;
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    if ($i > 0) {
        my str $fname = substr($s, 0, $i);
        if ($pkg ne "" && $pkg ne "repl" && $pkg ne "main") {
            return $pkg . "::" . $fname;
        }
        return $fname;
    }
    return "";
}

# Replace or add a function definition
private func register_function(str $func_def) int {
    my str $tagged_def = $func_def;
    if (!($tagged_def =~ /^\s*package\s+/)) {
        my str $tpkg = get_target_package();
        track_oop_package($tpkg);
        $tagged_def = "package " . $tpkg . ";\n" . $tagged_def;
    } elsif ($tagged_def =~ /^\s*package\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*)\s*;/) {
        my str $epkg = $tagged_def;
        $epkg =~ s/^\s*package\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*)\s*;[\s\S]*$/$1/;
        track_oop_package($epkg);
    }
    my str $name = get_function_name($tagged_def);
    if ($name eq "") {
        push(@g_functions, $tagged_def);
        return 0;
    }

    my int $i = 0;
    my int $count = scalar(@g_functions);
    while ($i < $count) {
        my str $existing_name = get_function_name($g_functions[$i]);
        if ($existing_name eq $name) {
            $g_functions[$i] = $tagged_def;
            return 1;
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    push(@g_functions, $tagged_def);
    return 0;
}

# Advance past a /regex/ or comment in JIT extract_function_def
private func jit_can_regex_after(str $c) int {
    if ($c eq ")" || $c eq "]" || $c eq "}" || $c eq "\"" || $c eq "'" || $c eq "_") { return 0; }
    if (($c ge "0" && $c le "9") || ($c ge "A" && $c le "Z") || ($c ge "a" && $c le "z")) { return 0; }
    return 1;
}

private func jit_is_ident_ch(str $c) int {
    if ($c eq "_") { return 1; }
    if (($c ge "0" && $c le "9") || ($c ge "A" && $c le "Z") || ($c ge "a" && $c le "z")) { return 1; }
    return 0;
}

private func jit_kw_allows_regex(str $w) int {
    if ($w eq "return" || $w eq "if" || $w eq "elsif" || $w eq "while" || $w eq "until" ||
        $w eq "unless" || $w eq "and" || $w eq "or" || $w eq "not" ||
        $w eq "eq" || $w eq "ne" || $w eq "lt" || $w eq "gt" || $w eq "le" || $w eq "ge" ||
        $w eq "cmp") {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

private func jit_skip_delimited_section(str $s, int $pos, int $len, int $allow_cc) int {
    if ($pos >= $len) {
        $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
        return $len;
    }
    my str $open = substr($s, $pos, 1);
    my str $close = $open;
    my int $paired = 0;
    if ($open eq "{") { $close = "}"; $paired = 1; }
    elsif ($open eq "(") { $close = ")"; $paired = 1; }
    elsif ($open eq "[") { $close = "]"; $paired = 1; }
    elsif ($open eq "<") { $close = ">"; $paired = 1; }
    my int $depth = 1;
    my int $in_class = 0;
    my int $cc_start = 0;
    my int $j = $pos + 1;
    while ($j < $len) {
        my str $ch = substr($s, $j, 1);
        if ($ch eq "\\" && $j + 1 < $len) { $j = $j + 2; next; }
        if ($allow_cc == 1 && $in_class == 1) {
            if ($ch eq "[" && $j + 1 < $len && substr($s, $j + 1, 1) eq ":") {
                my int $pend = index($s, ":]", $j + 2);
                if ($pend >= 0) { $j = $pend + 2; next; }
            }
            if ($ch eq "]" && $j > $cc_start && !($j == $cc_start + 1 && substr($s, $cc_start, 1) eq "^")) {
                $in_class = 0;
            }
            $j = $j + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($allow_cc == 1 && $ch eq "[") {
            $in_class = 1;
            $cc_start = $j + 1;
            $j = $j + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($paired == 1) {
            if ($ch eq $open) { $depth = $depth + 1; }
            elsif ($ch eq $close) {
                $depth = $depth - 1;
                if ($depth == 0) { return $j + 1; }
            }
        } else {
            if ($ch eq $open) { return $j + 1; }
        }
        $j = $j + 1;
    }
    $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
    return $len;
}

private func jit_try_skip_quote_op(str $s, int $pos, int $len) int {
    if ($pos > 0) {
        my str $prev = substr($s, $pos - 1, 1);
        if (jit_is_ident_ch($prev) == 1 || $prev eq "\$" || $prev eq "@" || $prev eq "%") {
            return -1;
        }
    }
    if ($pos >= 2) {
        my str $p2back = substr($s, $pos - 2, 2);
        if ($p2back eq "->" || $p2back eq "::") { return -1; }
    }
    my int $op_len = 0;
    my int $two_part = 0;
    my int $allow_cc1 = 0;
    if ($pos + 2 < $len) {
        my str $p2 = substr($s, $pos, 2);
        if ($p2 eq "qr") {
            $op_len = 2;
            $allow_cc1 = 1;
        } elsif ($p2 eq "qq" || $p2 eq "qw" || $p2 eq "qx") {
            $op_len = 2;
        } elsif ($p2 eq "tr") {
            $op_len = 2;
            $two_part = 1;
        }
    }
    if ($op_len == 0 && $pos < $len) {
        my str $p1 = substr($s, $pos, 1);
        if ($p1 eq "s") {
            $op_len = 1;
            $two_part = 1;
            $allow_cc1 = 1;
        } elsif ($p1 eq "y") {
            $op_len = 1;
            $two_part = 1;
        } elsif ($p1 eq "m") {
            $op_len = 1;
            $allow_cc1 = 1;
        } elsif ($p1 eq "q") {
            $op_len = 1;
        } else {
            return -1;
        }
    }
    my int $dpos = $pos + $op_len;
    if ($dpos >= $len) { return -1; }
    if ($dpos + 1 < $len) {
        my str $op2 = substr($s, $dpos, 2);
        if ($op2 eq "::" || $op2 eq "->") { return -1; }
    }
    my str $dc0 = substr($s, $dpos, 1);
    if (jit_is_ident_ch($dc0) == 1) { return -1; }
    my int $had_ws = 0;
    while ($dpos < $len) {
        my str $ws = substr($s, $dpos, 1);
        if ($ws eq " " || $ws eq "\t" || $ws eq "\r" || $ws eq "\n") {
            $had_ws = 1;
            $dpos = $dpos + 1;
        } else {
            last;
        }
    }
    if ($dpos >= $len) { return -1; }
    my str $delim = substr($s, $dpos, 1);
    if (jit_is_ident_ch($delim) == 1 || $delim eq "#") { return -1; }
    if ($delim eq ";" || $delim eq "," || $delim eq ")" || $delim eq "]" || $delim eq "}" || $delim eq "=") {
        return -1;
    }
    if ($had_ws == 1 && ($delim eq "+" || $delim eq "-" || $delim eq "*" || $delim eq "%" ||
                          $delim eq "&" || $delim eq "|" || $delim eq "^" || $delim eq "?" ||
                          $delim eq ":" || $delim eq "." || $delim eq ">" || $delim eq "<")) {
        return -1;
    }
    my int $is_paired = ($delim eq "{" || $delim eq "(" || $delim eq "[" || $delim eq "<") ? 1 : 0;
    my int $end1 = jit_skip_delimited_section($s, $dpos, $len, $allow_cc1);
    my int $fin = $end1;
    if ($two_part == 1) {
        if ($is_paired == 1) {
            my int $p2pos = $end1;
            while ($p2pos < $len) {
                my str $w2 = substr($s, $p2pos, 1);
                if ($w2 eq " " || $w2 eq "\t" || $w2 eq "\r" || $w2 eq "\n") {
                    $p2pos = $p2pos + 1;
                } else {
                    last;
                }
            }
            if ($p2pos < $len) {
                $fin = jit_skip_delimited_section($s, $p2pos, $len, 0);
            } else {
                $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
                $fin = $len;
            }
        } else {
            if ($end1 > $dpos + 1 && $end1 - 1 < $len && substr($s, $end1 - 1, 1) eq $delim) {
                $fin = jit_skip_delimited_section($s, $end1 - 1, $len, 0);
            } else {
                $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
            }
        }
    }
    while ($fin < $len) {
        my str $mc = substr($s, $fin, 1);
        if (($mc ge "a" && $mc le "z") || ($mc ge "A" && $mc le "Z")) {
            $fin = $fin + 1;
        } else {
            last;
        }
    }
    return $fin;
}

private func jit_skip_slash_token(str $input, int $pos, int $len, int $can_regex) int {
    if ($pos + 1 < $len && substr($input, $pos + 1, 1) eq "*") {
        my int $j = $pos + 2;
        while ($j + 1 < $len && !(substr($input, $j, 1) eq "*" && substr($input, $j + 1, 1) eq "/")) {
            $j = $j + 1;
        }
        if ($j + 1 < $len) { return $j + 2; }
        return $len;
    }
    if ($can_regex == 1) {
        my int $j = $pos + 1;
        my int $in_cc = 0;
        my int $cc_start = 0;
        while ($j < $len) {
            my str $rc = substr($input, $j, 1);
            if ($rc eq "\n") { last; }
            if ($rc eq "\\" && $j + 1 < $len) { $j = $j + 2; next; }
            if ($in_cc == 1) {
                if ($rc eq "[" && $j + 1 < $len && substr($input, $j + 1, 1) eq ":") {
                    my int $pend = index($input, ":]", $j + 2);
                    my int $nl = index($input, "\n", $j);
                    if ($pend >= 0 && ($nl < 0 || $nl > $pend)) { $j = $pend + 2; next; }
                }
                if ($rc eq "]" && $j > $cc_start && !($j == $cc_start + 1 && substr($input, $cc_start, 1) eq "^")) {
                    $in_cc = 0;
                }
                $j = $j + 1;
                next;
            }
            if ($rc eq "[") {
                $in_cc = 1;
                $cc_start = $j + 1;
            } elsif ($rc eq "/") {
                my int $end_p = $j + 1;
                while ($end_p < $len) {
                    my str $fc = substr($input, $end_p, 1);
                    if (($fc ge "a" && $fc le "z") || ($fc ge "A" && $fc le "Z")) {
                        $end_p = $end_p + 1;
                    } else {
                        last;
                    }
                }
                return $end_p;
            }
            $j = $j + 1;
        }
    }
    return $pos + 1;
}

# Extract function definition from input, returns array: [func_def, remainder].
# Brace matching runs on strip_strings_and_comments() output (same length,
# strings / comments / regexes / quote-ops / heredoc bodies blanked), so a `}`
# inside any of those never closes the body (V5-14). Falls back to the older
# token scanner if the stripper could not close something.
private func extract_function_def(str $input) array {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    my int $len = length($input);
    if ($g_strip_unclosed == 0 && length($cleaned) == $len) {
        my int $brace_pos = index($cleaned, "{");
        if ($brace_pos >= 0) {
            my int $depth = 0;
            my int $i = $brace_pos;
            my int $end_pos = -1;
            while ($i < $len) {
                my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
                if ($c eq "{") {
                    $depth = $depth + 1;
                } elsif ($c eq "}") {
                    $depth = $depth - 1;
                    if ($depth == 0) { $end_pos = $i; last; }
                }
                $i = $i + 1;
            }
            if ($end_pos >= 0) {
                my array @res = ("", "");
                $res[0] = substr($input, 0, $end_pos + 1);
                if ($end_pos + 1 < $len) {
                    my str $remainder = substr($input, $end_pos + 1, $len - $end_pos - 1);
                    $remainder =~ s/^\s*;\s*//;
                    $remainder =~ s/^\s+//;
                    $remainder =~ s/\s+$//;
                    $res[1] = $remainder;
                }
                return @res;
            }
        }
    }
    return extract_function_def_scan($input);
}

private func extract_function_def_scan(str $input) array {
    my array @result = ("", "");
    my int $len = length($input);
    my int $in_str = 0;
    my int $in_cmt = 0;
    my int $can_regex = 1;
    my int $brace_pos = -1;
    my int $scan = 0;

    while ($scan < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($input, $scan, 1);
        if ($in_cmt == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\n") { $in_cmt = 0; }
            $scan = $scan + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $scan + 1 < $len) { $scan = $scan + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $scan = $scan + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 2) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $scan + 1 < $len) { $scan = $scan + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $scan = $scan + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 1; $scan = $scan + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 2; $scan = $scan + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "#") { $in_cmt = 1; $scan = $scan + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "/") {
            my int $next_scan = jit_skip_slash_token($input, $scan, $len, $can_regex);
            if ($next_scan > $scan + 1) {
                $can_regex = 0;
                $scan = $next_scan;
                next;
            }
            $can_regex = 1;
            $scan = $scan + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "{") { $brace_pos = $scan; last; }
        my int $qend = jit_try_skip_quote_op($input, $scan, $len);
        if ($qend > $scan) {
            $can_regex = 0;
            $scan = $qend;
            next;
        }
        if (jit_is_ident_ch($c) == 1) {
            my int $ws = $scan;
            while ($ws < $len && jit_is_ident_ch(substr($input, $ws, 1)) == 1) {
                $ws = $ws + 1;
            }
            $can_regex = jit_kw_allows_regex(substr($input, $scan, $ws - $scan));
            $scan = $ws;
            next;
        }
        if ($c ne " " && $c ne "\t" && $c ne "\r" && $c ne "\n") {
            $can_regex = jit_can_regex_after($c);
        }
        $scan = $scan + 1;
    }

    if ($brace_pos < 0) {
        $result[0] = $input;
        return @result;
    }

    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $i = $brace_pos;
    $in_str = 0;
    $in_cmt = 0;
    $can_regex = 1;
    my int $end_pos = -1;

    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($input, $i, 1);

        if ($in_cmt == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\n") { $in_cmt = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) { $i = $i + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 2) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) { $i = $i + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }

        if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 2; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "#") { $in_cmt = 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "/") {
            my int $next_i = jit_skip_slash_token($input, $i, $len, $can_regex);
            if ($next_i > $i + 1) {
                $can_regex = 0;
                $i = $next_i;
                next;
            }
            $can_regex = 1;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }

        if ($c eq "{") {
            $depth = $depth + 1;
            $can_regex = 1;
        } elsif ($c eq "}") {
            $depth = $depth - 1;
            $can_regex = 0;
            if ($depth == 0) {
                $end_pos = $i;
                last;
            }
        } else {
            my int $qend2 = jit_try_skip_quote_op($input, $i, $len);
            if ($qend2 > $i) {
                $can_regex = 0;
                $i = $qend2;
                next;
            }
            if (jit_is_ident_ch($c) == 1) {
                my int $wi = $i;
                while ($wi < $len && jit_is_ident_ch(substr($input, $wi, 1)) == 1) {
                    $wi = $wi + 1;
                }
                $can_regex = jit_kw_allows_regex(substr($input, $i, $wi - $i));
                $i = $wi;
                next;
            }
            if ($c ne " " && $c ne "\t" && $c ne "\r" && $c ne "\n") {
                $can_regex = jit_can_regex_after($c);
            }
        }

        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    if ($end_pos >= 0) {
        $result[0] = substr($input, 0, $end_pos + 1);
        if ($end_pos + 1 < $len) {
            my str $remainder = substr($input, $end_pos + 1, $len - $end_pos - 1);
            $remainder =~ s/^\s*;\s*//;
            $remainder =~ s/^\s+//;
            $remainder =~ s/\s+$//;
            $result[1] = $remainder;
        }
    } else {
        $result[0] = $input;
    }

    return @result;
}

# Check if input is a package declaration
private func is_package_decl(str $input) int {
    if ($input =~ /^\s*package\s+[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Check if input is an OOP class declaration statement (has, extends, use overload)
private func is_oop_decl(str $input) int {
    if ($input =~ /^\s*(has|extends|inherit)\s+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($input =~ /^\s*use\s+overload\b/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Check if input is a use/import statement
private func is_import(str $input) int {
    if ($input =~ /^[ \t]*use[ \t]+overload\b/) {
        return 0;
    }
    if ($input =~ /^[ \t]*use[ \t]+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($input =~ /^[ \t]*import_lib[ \t]+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($input =~ /^[ \t]*import_object[ \t]+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($input =~ /^[ \t]*import_archive[ \t]+/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Register a use/import statement (avoid duplicates)
private func register_import(str $import_stmt) void {
    my str $normalized = $import_stmt;
    $normalized =~ s/[ \t]+$//;
    $normalized =~ s/;$//;
    $normalized =~ s/[ \t]+$//;

    # Handle "use lib" specially
    if ($normalized =~ /^use[ \t]+lib[ \t]+/) {
        my str $path = $normalized;
        $path =~ s/^use[ \t]+lib[ \t]+//;
        $path =~ s/^"//;
        $path =~ s/"$//;
        $path =~ s/^'//;
        $path =~ s/'$//;
        add_lib_path($path);
        return;
    }

    foreach my str $existing (@g_imports) {
        my str $existing_norm = $existing;
        $existing_norm =~ s/[ \t]+$//;
        $existing_norm =~ s/;$//;
        $existing_norm =~ s/[ \t]+$//;
        if ($existing_norm eq $normalized) {
            return;
        }
    }

    push(@g_imports, $normalized . ";");
}

private func jit_is_ident_char(str $c) int {
    if ($c eq "") { return 0; }
    my int $o = ord($c);
    if (($o >= 65 && $o <= 90) || ($o >= 97 && $o <= 122) || ($o >= 48 && $o <= 57) || $c eq "_") {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

private func jit_is_regex_prefix(str $prev_non_ws, str $prev_word) int {
    if ($prev_non_ws eq "") { return 1; }
    if (index("~([,{;=!?:&|", $prev_non_ws) >= 0) { return 1; }
    if ($prev_word eq "return" || $prev_word eq "if" || $prev_word eq "elsif" ||
        $prev_word eq "while" || $prev_word eq "unless" || $prev_word eq "when" ||
        $prev_word eq "and" || $prev_word eq "or" || $prev_word eq "not") {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

private func jit_is_heredoc_prefix(str $prev_non_ws, str $prev_word) int {
    if (jit_is_regex_prefix($prev_non_ws, $prev_word) == 1 || $prev_non_ws eq ".") {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($prev_word eq "say" || $prev_word eq "print" || $prev_word eq "warn" ||
        $prev_word eq "throw" || $prev_word eq "die" || $prev_word eq "push" ||
        $prev_word eq "unshift") {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

private func jit_decl_type_for(str $type_word, str $sigil) str {
    if ($sigil eq "@") { return "array"; }
    if ($sigil eq "%") { return "hash"; }
    if ($type_word eq "int" || $type_word eq "num" || $type_word eq "str" || $type_word eq "scalar") {
        return $type_word;
    }
    return "scalar";
}

private func jit_parse_my_paren(str $cleaned, int $open_pos) scalar {
    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    if ($open_pos >= $len || substr($cleaned, $open_pos, 1) ne "(") { return undef; }
    my int $p = $open_pos + 1;
    my array @vars = ();
    while ($p < $len) {
        while ($p < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $p, 1)) == 1) { $p = $p + 1; }
        if ($p >= $len) { return undef; }
        if (substr($cleaned, $p, 1) eq ")") {
            if (size(@vars) == 0) { return undef; }
            return { "end" => $p + 1, "vars" => \@vars };
        }
        my int $wstart = $p;
        my str $word = "";
        while ($p < $len && (substr($cleaned, $p, 1) =~ /[A-Za-z0-9_:]/)) {
            $word = $word . substr($cleaned, $p, 1);
            $p = $p + 1;
        }
        if ($word ne "") {
            while ($p < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $p, 1)) == 1) { $p = $p + 1; }
        } else {
            $p = $wstart;
        }
        if ($p >= $len) { return undef; }
        my str $sigil = substr($cleaned, $p, 1);
        if ($sigil ne "\$" && $sigil ne "@" && $sigil ne "%") {
            return undef;
        }
        $p = $p + 1;
        my str $vname = "";
        while ($p < $len && (substr($cleaned, $p, 1) =~ /[A-Za-z0-9_]/)) {
            $vname = $vname . substr($cleaned, $p, 1);
            $p = $p + 1;
        }
        if ($vname eq "") { return undef; }
        push(@vars, { "sigil" => $sigil, "type" => jit_decl_type_for($word, $sigil), "name" => $vname });
        while ($p < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $p, 1)) == 1) { $p = $p + 1; }
        if ($p >= $len) { return undef; }
        my str $sep = substr($cleaned, $p, 1);
        if ($sep eq ",") {
            $p = $p + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($sep eq ")") {
            return { "end" => $p + 1, "vars" => \@vars };
        }
        return undef;
    }
    return undef;
}

private func jit_matching_delim(str $open_d) str {
    if ($open_d eq "{") { return "}"; }
    if ($open_d eq "(") { return ")"; }
    if ($open_d eq "[") { return "]"; }
    if ($open_d eq "<") { return ">"; }
    return $open_d;
}

private func jit_scan_delim_body(str $s, int $pos, str $open_d, str $close_d, int $allow_char_class, int $allow_newline) int {
    my int $len = length($s);
    my int $i = $pos;
    my int $paired = ($open_d ne $close_d) ? 1 : 0;
    my int $nest = 1;
    my int $in_class = 0;
    my int $cc_start = 0;
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($s, $i, 1);
        if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) {
            $i = $i + 2;
            next;
        }
        if ($allow_newline == 0 && $c eq "\n") {
            return -1;
        }
        if ($allow_char_class == 1 && $in_class == 1) {
            if ($c eq "[" && $i + 1 < $len && substr($s, $i + 1, 1) eq ":") {
                my int $pend = index($s, ":]", $i + 2);
                if ($pend >= 0) {
                    my int $nl = ($allow_newline == 0) ? index($s, "\n", $i) : -1;
                    if ($nl < 0 || $nl > $pend) {
                        $i = $pend + 2;
                        next;
                    }
                }
            }
            if ($c eq "]" && $i > $cc_start && !($i == $cc_start + 1 && substr($s, $cc_start, 1) eq "^")) {
                $in_class = 0;
            }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($allow_char_class == 1 && $c eq "[") {
            $in_class = 1;
            $cc_start = $i + 1;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($paired == 1 && $c eq $open_d) {
            $nest = $nest + 1;
        } elsif ($c eq $close_d) {
            $nest = $nest - 1;
            if ($nest == 0) {
                return $i + 1;
            }
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return -1;
}

private func skip_regex_literal(str $s, int $pos, str $prev_non_ws, str $prev_word) int {
    my int $len = length($s);
    if ($pos >= $len) { return -1; }
    my str $c = substr($s, $pos, 1);

    if ($c eq "/") {
        if (jit_is_regex_prefix($prev_non_ws, $prev_word) == 0) { return -1; }
        if ($pos + 1 < $len && substr($s, $pos + 1, 1) eq "/" && $prev_non_ws ne "~") { return -1; }
        my int $end_p = jit_scan_delim_body($s, $pos + 1, "/", "/", 1, 0);
        if ($end_p < 0) { return -1; }
        while ($end_p < $len && substr($s, $end_p, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z]/) {
            $end_p = $end_p + 1;
        }
        return $end_p;
    }

    if ($prev_word eq "func") {
        return -1;
    }
    return jit_try_skip_quote_op($s, $pos, $len);
}

# Replace string literals, regex literals, and # comments with spaces so scans never false-positive
private func strip_strings_and_comments(str $input) str {
    $g_strip_unclosed = 0;
    @g_last_heredoc_ranges = ();
    my str $out = "";
    my int $len = length($input);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $in_str = 0;
    my int $in_cmt = 0;
    my str $prev_non_ws = "";
    my str $cur_word = "";
    my str $last_word = "";
    my array @heredoc_tags = ();
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($input, $i, 1);
        if ($in_cmt == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\n") {
                $in_cmt = 0;
                if (size(@heredoc_tags) == 0) {
                    $out = $out . "\n";
                    $i = $i + 1;
                    next;
                }
            } else {
                $out = $out . " ";
                $i = $i + 1;
                next;
            }
        }
        if ($in_cmt == 2) {
            if ($c eq "*" && $i + 1 < $len && substr($input, $i + 1, 1) eq "/") {
                $in_cmt = 0;
                $out = $out . "  ";
                $i = $i + 2;
                next;
            }
            $out = $out . (($c eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) {
                my str $n2 = substr($input, $i + 1, 1);
                $out = $out . " " . (($n2 eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
                $i = $i + 2;
                next;
            }
            if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 0; $prev_non_ws = "\""; }
            $out = $out . (($c eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 2) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) {
                my str $n2 = substr($input, $i + 1, 1);
                $out = $out . " " . (($n2 eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
                $i = $i + 2;
                next;
            }
            if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 0; $prev_non_ws = "'"; }
            $out = $out . (($c eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "\n" && size(@heredoc_tags) > 0) {
            my int $hdr_nl = $i;
            $out = $out . "\n";
            $i = $i + 1;
            while (size(@heredoc_tags) > 0) {
                my str $htag = shift(@heredoc_tags);
                while (1) {
                    if ($i >= $len) {
                        $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
                        last;
                    }
                    my int $nl = index($input, "\n", $i);
                    if ($nl < 0) {
                        my str $hline = substr($input, $i, $len - $i);
                        if (length($hline) > 0 && substr($hline, length($hline) - 1, 1) eq "\r") {
                            $hline = substr($hline, 0, length($hline) - 1);
                        }
                        $out = $out . (" " x ($len - $i));
                        $i = $len;
                        if ($hline ne $htag || size(@heredoc_tags) > 0) {
                            $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
                        }
                        last;
                    }
                    my str $hline = substr($input, $i, $nl - $i);
                    if (length($hline) > 0 && substr($hline, length($hline) - 1, 1) eq "\r") {
                        $hline = substr($hline, 0, length($hline) - 1);
                    }
                    $out = $out . (" " x ($nl - $i)) . "\n";
                    $i = $nl + 1;
                    if ($hline eq $htag) {
                        last;
                    }
                    if (substr($htag, 0, 1) eq "~" && trim($hline) eq substr($htag, 1, length($htag) - 1)) {
                        last;
                    }
                }
                if ($g_strip_unclosed == 1) {
                    last;
                }
            }
            push(@g_last_heredoc_ranges, [$hdr_nl, ($i > 0 ? $i - 1 : 0)]);
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 1; $cur_word = ""; $out = $out . " "; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 2; $cur_word = ""; $out = $out . " "; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "#") {
            $in_cmt = 1;
            if ($cur_word ne "") { $last_word = $cur_word; $cur_word = ""; }
            $out = $out . " ";
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "/" && $i + 1 < $len && substr($input, $i + 1, 1) eq "*") {
            $in_cmt = 2;
            if ($cur_word ne "") { $last_word = $cur_word; $cur_word = ""; }
            $out = $out . "  ";
            $i = $i + 2;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "<" && $i + 1 < $len && substr($input, $i + 1, 1) eq "<" &&
            jit_is_heredoc_prefix($prev_non_ws, ($cur_word ne "" ? $cur_word : $last_word)) == 1) {
            my int $hp = $i + 2;
            my int $hend = -1;
            my str $htag = "";
            # <<~TAG: the terminator may be indented (tag kept as "~TAG");
            # <<\TAG: literal
            my str $h_tl = "";
            if ($hp < $len && substr($input, $hp, 1) eq "~") { $h_tl = "~"; $hp = $hp + 1; }
            if ($hp < $len && substr($input, $hp, 1) eq "\\") { $hp = $hp + 1; }
            if ($hp < $len) {
                my str $hc0 = substr($input, $hp, 1);
                if (jit_is_ident_char($hc0) == 1 && !($hc0 ge "0" && $hc0 le "9")) {
                    my int $he = $hp + 1;
                    while ($he < $len && jit_is_ident_char(substr($input, $he, 1)) == 1) {
                        $he = $he + 1;
                    }
                    $htag = substr($input, $hp, $he - $hp);
                    $hend = $he;
                } else {
                    my int $qp = $hp;
                    while ($qp < $len && (substr($input, $qp, 1) eq " " || substr($input, $qp, 1) eq "\t")) {
                        $qp = $qp + 1;
                    }
                    if ($qp < $len) {
                        my str $qc = substr($input, $qp, 1);
                        if ($qc eq "'" || $qc eq "\"") {
                            my int $qe = $qp + 1;
                            while ($qe < $len && substr($input, $qe, 1) ne $qc && substr($input, $qe, 1) ne "\n") {
                                $qe = $qe + 1;
                            }
                            if ($qe < $len && substr($input, $qe, 1) eq $qc && $qe > $qp + 1) {
                                $htag = substr($input, $qp + 1, $qe - ($qp + 1));
                                $hend = $qe + 1;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            if ($hend > $i) {
                push(@heredoc_tags, $h_tl . $htag);
                $out = $out . (" " x ($hend - $i));
                $prev_non_ws = "\"";
                $cur_word = "";
                $last_word = "";
                $i = $hend;
                next;
            }
        }

        my int $rx_end = skip_regex_literal($input, $i, $prev_non_ws, ($cur_word ne "" ? $cur_word : $last_word));
        if ($rx_end > $i) {
            my int $ri = $i;
            while ($ri < $rx_end) {
                my str $rc = substr($input, $ri, 1);
                $out = $out . (($rc eq "\n") ? "\n" : " ");
                $ri = $ri + 1;
            }
            $prev_non_ws = "/";
            $cur_word = "";
            $last_word = "";
            $i = $rx_end;
            next;
        }

        if (jit_is_ident_char($c) == 1) {
            $cur_word = $cur_word . $c;
            $last_word = $cur_word;
            $prev_non_ws = $c;
        } elsif ($c eq " " || $c eq "\t" || $c eq "\n" || $c eq "\r") {
            if ($cur_word ne "") {
                $last_word = $cur_word;
                $cur_word = "";
            }
        } else {
            if ($cur_word ne "") {
                $last_word = $cur_word;
                $cur_word = "";
            } else {
                $last_word = "";
            }
            $prev_non_ws = $c;
        }
        $out = $out . $c;
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    if ($in_str != 0 || $in_cmt == 2 || size(@heredoc_tags) > 0) {
        $g_strip_unclosed = 1;
    }
    return $out;
}

private func jit_is_ws(str $ch) int {
    return ($ch eq " " || $ch eq "\t" || $ch eq "\n" || $ch eq "\r") ? 1 : 0;
}

# Check if input declares a specific variable at top level (brace/paren/bracket depth 0)
private func input_declares_var(str $input, str $name, str $sigil) int {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $pdepth = 0;
    my int $bdepth = 0;
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        if ($c eq "{") { $depth = $depth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "}") { $depth = $depth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "(") { $pdepth = $pdepth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq ")") { $pdepth = $pdepth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "[") { $bdepth = $bdepth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "]") { $bdepth = $bdepth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($depth == 0 && $pdepth == 0 && $bdepth == 0 && $c eq "m" && $i + 2 < $len && substr($cleaned, $i + 1, 1) eq "y") {
            my str $after_my = substr($cleaned, $i + 2, 1);
            my int $prev_ok = ($i == 0 || jit_is_ident_char(substr($cleaned, $i - 1, 1)) == 0) ? 1 : 0;
            if ($prev_ok == 1 && jit_is_ws($after_my) == 1) {
                my int $pos = $i + 2;
                while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) {
                    $pos = $pos + 1;
                }
                my int $wstart = $pos;
                my str $word = "";
                while ($pos < $len && (substr($cleaned, $pos, 1) =~ /[A-Za-z0-9_:]/)) {
                    $word = $word . substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                    $pos = $pos + 1;
                }
                if ($word ne "") {
                    while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) {
                        $pos = $pos + 1;
                    }
                    if ($pos < $len) {
                        my str $sc = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                        if ($sc ne "\$" && $sc ne "@" && $sc ne "%") {
                            $pos = $wstart;
                        }
                    } else {
                        $pos = $wstart;
                    }
                }
                if ($pos < $len && substr($cleaned, $pos, 1) eq "(") {
                    my scalar $pd = jit_parse_my_paren($cleaned, $pos);
                    if (defined($pd)) {
                        my array @vars = @{$pd->{"vars"}};
                        my int $vi = 0;
                        while ($vi < size(@vars)) {
                            if ($vars[$vi]->{"sigil"} eq $sigil && $vars[$vi]->{"name"} eq $name) {
                                return 1;
                            }
                            $vi = $vi + 1;
                        }
                        $i = $pd->{"end"};
                        next;
                    }
                }
                if ($pos < $len && substr($cleaned, $pos, 1) eq $sigil) {
                    $pos = $pos + 1;
                    my str $vname = "";
                    while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ident_char(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) {
                        $vname = $vname . substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                        $pos = $pos + 1;
                    }
                    if ($vname eq $name) {
                        return 1;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# Register variables from input (only at brace/paren/bracket depth 0, skipping strings, comments & regexes)
private func register_variables(str $input) void {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $pdepth = 0;
    my int $bdepth = 0;

    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);

        if ($c eq "{") { $depth = $depth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "}") { $depth = $depth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "(") { $pdepth = $pdepth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq ")") { $pdepth = $pdepth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "[") { $bdepth = $bdepth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "]") { $bdepth = $bdepth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }

        if ($depth == 0 && $pdepth == 0 && $bdepth == 0 && $c eq "m" && $i + 2 < $len && substr($cleaned, $i + 1, 1) eq "y") {
            my str $after_my = substr($cleaned, $i + 2, 1);
            my int $word_ok = 0;
            if (jit_is_ws($after_my) == 1) {
                if ($i == 0) {
                    $word_ok = 1;
                } else {
                    my str $prev = substr($cleaned, $i - 1, 1);
                    if (!($prev =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_]/)) { $word_ok = 1; }
                }
            }
            if ($word_ok == 1) {
                my int $pos = $i + 2;
                while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) {
                    $pos = $pos + 1;
                }
                my str $type = "scalar";
                my int $word_start = $pos;
                my str $next_word = "";
                while ($pos < $len) {
                    my str $wc = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                    if ($wc =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_:]/) {
                        $next_word = $next_word . $wc;
                        $pos = $pos + 1;
                    } else {
                        last;
                    }
                }
                if ($next_word eq "int" || $next_word eq "num" || $next_word eq "str" || $next_word eq "scalar" || $next_word eq "array" || $next_word eq "hash") {
                    $type = $next_word;
                    while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) {
                        $pos = $pos + 1;
                    }
                } elsif ($next_word ne "") {
                    my int $look = $pos;
                    while ($look < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $look, 1)) == 1) {
                        $look = $look + 1;
                    }
                    if ($look < $len) {
                        my str $sc = substr($cleaned, $look, 1);
                        if ($sc eq "\$" || $sc eq "@" || $sc eq "%") {
                            $pos = $look;
                        } else {
                            $pos = $word_start;
                        }
                    } else {
                        $pos = $word_start;
                    }
                } else {
                    $pos = $word_start;
                }
                if ($pos < $len) {
                    my str $sigil = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                    if ($sigil eq "(") {
                        my scalar $pd = jit_parse_my_paren($cleaned, $pos);
                        if (defined($pd)) {
                            my array @vars = @{$pd->{"vars"}};
                            my int $vi = 0;
                            while ($vi < size(@vars)) {
                                $g_var_types{jit_vk("" . $vars[$vi]->{"type"}, "" . $vars[$vi]->{"name"})} = $vars[$vi]->{"type"};
                                $vi = $vi + 1;
                            }
                            $i = $pd->{"end"};
                            next;
                        }
                    }
                    if ($sigil eq "\$" || $sigil eq "@" || $sigil eq "%") {
                        if ($sigil eq "@") { $type = "array"; }
                        if ($sigil eq "%") { $type = "hash"; }
                        $pos = $pos + 1;
                        my str $name = "";
                        while ($pos < $len && (substr($cleaned, $pos, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_]/)) {
                            $name = $name . substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                            $pos = $pos + 1;
                        }
                        if ($name ne "") {
                            $g_var_types{jit_vk($type, $name)} = $type;
                        }
                        $i = $pos;
                        next;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
}

# Record top-level `our [TYPE] SIGILname` / `our (...)` declarations. They are
# re-declared at package level in every later eval's source, so later
# snippets (and functions) see the variable; the value lives in the global
# registry and persists by itself (V5-11).
private func register_our_decls(str $input) void {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    my str $pkg = get_target_package();
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        if ($c eq "{" || $c eq "(" || $c eq "[") { $depth = $depth + 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "}" || $c eq ")" || $c eq "]") { $depth = $depth - 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($depth == 0 && $c eq "o" && $i + 3 < $len && substr($cleaned, $i, 3) eq "our"
            && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $i + 3, 1)) == 1
            && ($i == 0 || jit_is_ident_char(substr($cleaned, $i - 1, 1)) == 0)) {
            my int $pos = $i + 3;
            while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) { $pos = $pos + 1; }
            my str $type = "";
            my int $ws = $pos;
            while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ident_char(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) { $pos = $pos + 1; }
            my str $word = substr($cleaned, $ws, $pos - $ws);
            if ($word eq "int" || $word eq "num" || $word eq "str" || $word eq "scalar" || $word eq "array" || $word eq "hash") {
                $type = $word;
                while ($pos < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $pos, 1)) == 1) { $pos = $pos + 1; }
            } else {
                $pos = $ws;
            }
            my array @found = ();
            if ($pos < $len && substr($cleaned, $pos, 1) eq "(") {
                my scalar $pd = jit_parse_my_paren($cleaned, $pos);
                if (defined($pd)) {
                    foreach my scalar $v (@{$pd->{"vars"}}) {
                        push(@found, [$v->{"sigil"}, $v->{"name"}, ""]);
                    }
                    $i = $pd->{"end"};
                }
            } elsif ($pos < $len) {
                my str $sg = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
                if ($sg eq "\$" || $sg eq "@" || $sg eq "%") {
                    my int $ns = $pos + 1;
                    my int $ne = $ns;
                    while ($ne < $len && jit_is_ident_char(substr($cleaned, $ne, 1)) == 1) { $ne = $ne + 1; }
                    if ($ne > $ns) {
                        push(@found, [$sg, substr($cleaned, $ns, $ne - $ns), $type]);
                    }
                    $i = $ne;
                }
            }
            foreach my scalar $f (@found) {
                my str $sg = $f->[0];
                my str $t = $f->[2];
                if ($sg eq "@") { $t = "array"; }
                elsif ($sg eq "%") { $t = "hash"; }
                elsif ($t eq "" || $t eq "array" || $t eq "hash") { $t = "scalar"; }
                my str $key = $pkg . "::" . $sg . $f->[1];
                my str $entry = "package " . $pkg . ";\nour " . $t . " " . $sg . $f->[1] . ";";
                if (exists($g_our_decl_idx{$key})) {
                    $g_our_decls[$g_our_decl_idx{$key}] = $entry;
                } else {
                    $g_our_decl_idx{$key} = scalar(@g_our_decls);
                    push(@g_our_decls, $entry);
                }
            }
            if ($i < $pos) { $i = $pos; }
            next;
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
}

# Convert my declarations to our in user code for variable persistence
# Only converts at brace depth 0 — declarations inside blocks stay as 'my'
private func convert_my_to_our(str $input) str {
    my str $result = "";
    my int $len = length($input);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $in_str = 0;
    my int $in_cmt = 0;

    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($input, $i, 1);

        if ($in_cmt == 1) {
            $result = $result . $c;
            if ($c eq "\n") { $in_cmt = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) {
                $result = $result . substr($input, $i, 2);
                $i = $i + 2;
                next;
            }
            if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 0; }
            $result = $result . $c;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 2) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) {
                $result = $result . substr($input, $i, 2);
                $i = $i + 2;
                next;
            }
            if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 0; }
            $result = $result . $c;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }

        if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 2; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "#") { $in_cmt = 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }

        # Track brace depth
        if ($c eq "{") {
            $depth = $depth + 1;
            $result = $result . $c;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "}") {
            $depth = $depth - 1;
            $result = $result . $c;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }

        # At depth > 0, copy through unchanged
        if ($depth > 0) {
            $result = $result . $c;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }

        # At depth 0, check for "my" keyword at word boundary
        if ($c eq "m" && $i + 2 < $len && substr($input, $i + 1, 1) eq "y") {
            my str $after_my = substr($input, $i + 2, 1);
            # Check word boundary: "my" must be followed by space or tab
            if ($after_my eq " " || $after_my eq "\t") {
                # Check that "my" is at start or preceded by non-word char
                my int $is_word_start = 0;
                if ($i == 0) {
                    $is_word_start = 1;
                } else {
                    my str $before = substr($input, $i - 1, 1);
                    if (!($before =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_]/)) {
                        $is_word_start = 1;
                    }
                }

                if ($is_word_start == 1) {
                    # Look ahead to determine the declaration pattern
                    my int $j = $i + 2;
                    while ($j < $len && (substr($input, $j, 1) eq " " || substr($input, $j, 1) eq "\t")) {
                        $j = $j + 1;
                    }
                    if ($j < $len) {
                        my str $next = substr($input, $j, 1);
                        if ($next eq "$" || $next eq "@" || $next eq "%") {
                            if ($next eq "$") {
                                $result = $result . "our scalar ";
                            } elsif ($next eq "@") {
                                $result = $result . "our array ";
                            } else {
                                $result = $result . "our hash ";
                            }
                            $i = $i + 2;
                            while ($i < $len && (substr($input, $i, 1) eq " " || substr($input, $i, 1) eq "\t")) {
                                $i = $i + 1;
                            }
                            next;
                        } else {
                            $result = $result . "our";
                            $i = $i + 2;
                            next;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        $result = $result . $c;
        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    return $result;
}

private func first_toplevel_semi(str $s) int {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($s);
    my int $n = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    while ($i < $n) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        if ($c eq "{" || $c eq "(" || $c eq "[") { $depth = $depth + 1; }
        elsif ($c eq "}" || $c eq ")" || $c eq "]") { $depth = $depth - 1; }
        elsif ($c eq ";" && $depth == 0) { return $i; }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return -1;
}

# Index of the last top-level ';' in $s that has non-whitespace content after
# it, or -1 if there is none. Respects strings, regexes, # comments, and (){}[] nesting.
private func last_toplevel_semi(str $s) int {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($s);
    my int $n = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $last_semi = -1;
    my int $pending_semi = -1;
    my int $hri = 0;
    my int $hrc = size(@g_last_heredoc_ranges);
    while ($i < $n) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        if ($pending_semi >= 0 && $i > $pending_semi && $c ne " " && $c ne "\t" && $c ne "\n" && $c ne "\r") {
            $last_semi = $pending_semi;
            $pending_semi = -1;
        }
        if ($c eq "{" || $c eq "(" || $c eq "[") { $depth = $depth + 1; }
        elsif ($c eq "}" || $c eq ")" || $c eq "]") { $depth = $depth - 1; }
        elsif ($c eq ";" && $depth == 0) {
            while ($hri < $hrc && $g_last_heredoc_ranges[$hri]->[0] < $i) {
                $hri = $hri + 1;
            }
            if ($hri < $hrc) {
                my int $line_nl = index($s, "\n", $i);
                if ($line_nl >= 0 && $g_last_heredoc_ranges[$hri]->[0] == $line_nl) {
                    $pending_semi = $g_last_heredoc_ranges[$hri]->[1];
                } else {
                    $pending_semi = $i;
                }
            } else {
                $pending_semi = $i;
            }
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return $last_semi;
}

# End index (position of closing '}') of a leading top-level control-flow block
# statement when non-whitespace expression tokens follow it without ';', else -1.
private func leading_block_stmt_end(str $s) int {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($s);
    my int $n = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    while ($i < $n && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $i, 1)) == 1) {
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    my str $kw = "";
    my int $ki = $i;
    while ($ki < $n && (substr($cleaned, $ki, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z_]/)) {
        $kw = $kw . substr($cleaned, $ki, 1);
        $ki = $ki + 1;
    }
    if ($kw ne "if" && $kw ne "unless" && $kw ne "while" && $kw ne "until" &&
        $kw ne "for" && $kw ne "foreach" && $kw ne "switch" && $kw ne "try") {
        return -1;
    }
    if ($ki < $n && (substr($cleaned, $ki, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_:]/)) {
        return -1;
    }
    my int $pos = $ki;
    while (1) {
        my int $pdepth = 0;
        my int $found_brace = 0;
        while ($pos < $n) {
            my str $ch = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
            if ($ch eq "(" || $ch eq "[") { $pdepth = $pdepth + 1; }
            elsif ($ch eq ")" || $ch eq "]") { $pdepth = $pdepth - 1; }
            elsif ($ch eq "{" && $pdepth == 0) { $found_brace = 1; last; }
            elsif ($ch eq ";" && $pdepth == 0) { return -1; }
            $pos = $pos + 1;
        }
        if ($found_brace == 0) { return -1; }
        my int $bdepth = 0;
        my int $close_idx = -1;
        while ($pos < $n) {
            my str $ch = substr($cleaned, $pos, 1);
            if ($ch eq "{") { $bdepth = $bdepth + 1; }
            elsif ($ch eq "}") {
                $bdepth = $bdepth - 1;
                if ($bdepth == 0) { $close_idx = $pos; $pos = $pos + 1; last; }
            }
            $pos = $pos + 1;
        }
        if ($close_idx < 0) { return -1; }
        my int $after = $pos;
        while ($after < $n && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $after, 1)) == 1) {
            $after = $after + 1;
        }
        if ($after >= $n) {
            return -1;
        }
        my str $next_kw = "";
        my int $nki = $after;
        while ($nki < $n && (substr($cleaned, $nki, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z_]/)) {
            $next_kw = $next_kw . substr($cleaned, $nki, 1);
            $nki = $nki + 1;
        }
        my int $next_boundary = ($nki >= $n || !(substr($cleaned, $nki, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_:]/)) ? 1 : 0;
        if ($next_boundary == 1 && ($next_kw eq "elsif" || $next_kw eq "else" || $next_kw eq "catch" || $next_kw eq "finally")) {
            $pos = $nki;
            next;
        }
        return $close_idx;
    }
    return -1;
}

# Strip top-level (depth 0) `my [TYPE] SIGIL+name` prefixes so declarations
# inside the wrapped helper closure assign to repl_eval()'s captured locals
# instead of shadowing them inside the closure.
private func strip_toplevel_my(str $input) str {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    my str $result = "";
    my int $len = length($input);
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $pdepth = 0;
    my int $bdepth = 0;

    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $cc = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        my str $c = substr($input, $i, 1);

        if ($cc eq "{") { $depth = $depth + 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($cc eq "}") { $depth = $depth - 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($cc eq "(") { $pdepth = $pdepth + 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($cc eq ")") { $pdepth = $pdepth - 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($cc eq "[") { $bdepth = $bdepth + 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($cc eq "]") { $bdepth = $bdepth - 1; $result = $result . $c; $i = $i + 1; next; }

        if ($depth == 0 && $pdepth == 0 && $bdepth == 0 && $cc eq "m" && $i + 2 < $len && substr($cleaned, $i + 1, 1) eq "y") {
            my str $after_my = substr($cleaned, $i + 2, 1);
            if (jit_is_ws($after_my) == 1) {
                my int $word_ok = 0;
                if ($i == 0) {
                    $word_ok = 1;
                } else {
                    my str $prev = substr($cleaned, $i - 1, 1);
                    if (!($prev =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_]/)) {
                        $word_ok = 1;
                    }
                }
                if ($word_ok == 1) {
                    my int $j = $i + 2;
                    while ($j < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $j, 1)) == 1) {
                        $j = $j + 1;
                    }
                    my str $vtype = "scalar";
                    my int $wstart = $j;
                    my str $word = "";
                    while ($j < $len) {
                        my str $wc = substr($cleaned, $j, 1);
                        if ($wc =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_:]/) {
                            $word = $word . $wc;
                            $j = $j + 1;
                        } else {
                            last;
                        }
                    }
                    if ($word eq "int" || $word eq "num" || $word eq "str" || $word eq "scalar" || $word eq "array" || $word eq "hash") {
                        $vtype = $word;
                        while ($j < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $j, 1)) == 1) {
                            $j = $j + 1;
                        }
                    } elsif ($word ne "") {
                        my int $look = $j;
                        while ($look < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $look, 1)) == 1) {
                            $look = $look + 1;
                        }
                        if ($look < $len) {
                            my str $sc = substr($cleaned, $look, 1);
                            if ($sc eq "\$" || $sc eq "@" || $sc eq "%") {
                                $j = $look;
                            } else {
                                $j = $wstart;
                            }
                        } else {
                            $j = $wstart;
                        }
                    } else {
                        $j = $wstart;
                    }
                    if ($j < $len) {
                        my str $sigil = substr($cleaned, $j, 1);
                        if ($sigil eq "(") {
                            my scalar $pd = jit_parse_my_paren($cleaned, $j);
                            if (defined($pd)) {
                                my array @vars = @{$pd->{"vars"}};
                                my array @parts = ();
                                my int $vi = 0;
                                while ($vi < size(@vars)) {
                                    push(@parts, $vars[$vi]->{"sigil"} . $vars[$vi]->{"name"});
                                    $vi = $vi + 1;
                                }
                                $result = $result . "(" . join(", ", @parts) . ")";
                                $i = $pd->{"end"};
                                next;
                            }
                        }
                        if ($sigil eq "$" || $sigil eq "@" || $sigil eq "%") {
                            $j = $j + 1;
                            my str $vname = "";
                            while ($j < $len && (substr($cleaned, $j, 1) =~ /[a-zA-Z0-9_]/)) {
                                $vname = $vname . substr($cleaned, $j, 1);
                                $j = $j + 1;
                            }
                            if ($vname ne "") {
                                if ($sigil eq "%") {
                                    my int $rp = length($result) - 1;
                                    while ($rp >= 0 && jit_is_ws(substr($result, $rp, 1)) == 1) {
                                        $rp = $rp - 1;
                                    }
                                    if ($rp >= 0 && substr($result, $rp, 1) eq "}") {
                                        $result = $result . "; ";
                                    }
                                }
                                my int $k = $j;
                                while ($k < $len && jit_is_ws(substr($cleaned, $k, 1)) == 1) {
                                    $k = $k + 1;
                                }
                                if ($k == $len || substr($cleaned, $k, 1) eq ";") {
                                    # Standalone `my int $x;` -> reset to default value
                                    my str $defv = "undef";
                                    if ($sigil eq "@" || $sigil eq "%") { $defv = "()"; }
                                    elsif ($vtype eq "int") { $defv = "0"; }
                                    elsif ($vtype eq "num") { $defv = "0.0"; }
                                    elsif ($vtype eq "str") { $defv = "\"\""; }
                                    $result = $result . $sigil . $vname . " = " . $defv;
                                    $i = $k;
                                    next;
                                } else {
                                    # `my int $x = expr` -> `$x = expr`
                                    $result = $result . $sigil . $vname;
                                    $i = $j;
                                    next;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        $result = $result . $c;
        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    return $result;
}

# Find matching closer (e.g. ')' or '}') starting at $open_pos; return index or -1
private func jit_find_matching(str $s, int $open_pos, str $open_ch, str $close_ch) int {
    my int $len = length($s);
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $in_str = 0;
    my int $in_cmt = 0;
    my int $can_regex = 1;
    my int $i = $open_pos;
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($s, $i, 1);
        if ($in_cmt == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\n") { $in_cmt = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 1) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) { $i = $i + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($in_str == 2) {
            if ($c eq "\\" && $i + 1 < $len) { $i = $i + 2; next; }
            if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 0; $can_regex = 0; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "\"") { $in_str = 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "'") { $in_str = 2; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq "#") { $in_cmt = 1; $i = $i + 1; next; }
        if ($c eq $open_ch) {
            $depth = $depth + 1;
            $can_regex = 1;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq $close_ch) {
            $depth = $depth - 1;
            $can_regex = 0;
            if ($depth == 0) { return $i; }
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "/") {
            my int $next_i = jit_skip_slash_token($s, $i, $len, $can_regex);
            if ($next_i > $i + 1) {
                $can_regex = 0;
                $i = $next_i;
                next;
            }
            $can_regex = 1;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        my int $qend = jit_try_skip_quote_op($s, $i, $len);
        if ($qend > $i) {
            $can_regex = 0;
            $i = $qend;
            next;
        }
        if (jit_is_ident_ch($c) == 1) {
            my int $wi = $i;
            while ($wi < $len && jit_is_ident_ch(substr($s, $wi, 1)) == 1) {
                $wi = $wi + 1;
            }
            $can_regex = jit_kw_allows_regex(substr($s, $i, $wi - $i));
            $i = $wi;
            next;
        }
        if ($c ne " " && $c ne "\t" && $c ne "\r" && $c ne "\n") {
            if ($c eq "(" || $c eq "[" || $c eq "{") { $can_regex = 1; }
            else { $can_regex = jit_can_regex_after($c); }
        }
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return -1;
}

private func jit_is_complete_call(str $trimmed, int $open_pos) int {
    my int $close_pos = jit_find_matching($trimmed, $open_pos, "(", ")");
    if ($close_pos < 0) { return 0; }
    my str $tail = substr($trimmed, $close_pos + 1, length($trimmed) - $close_pos - 1);
    if ($tail =~ /^\s*;?\s*(?:#.*)?$/) { return 1; }
    return 0;
}

# Generate Strada source wrapping user code
private func generate_source(str $input) str {
    my str $src = "";

    # Import statements
    foreach my str $imp (@g_imports) {
        $src = $src . $imp . "\n";
    }
    if (scalar(@g_imports) > 0) {
        $src = $src . "\n";
    }

    # Always use repl package for variable persistence via global registry
    $src = $src . "package repl;\n\n";
    $src = $src . "__C__ {\n    static StradaValue ***__repl_caps = NULL;\n    static StradaValue ****__repl_caps_stack = NULL;\n    static int __repl_caps_sp = 0;\n    static int __repl_caps_cap = 0;\n}\n\n";

    # Constants, enums, and OOP class declarations (must be at package level)
    foreach my str $const_decl (@g_constants) {
        $src = $src . $const_decl . "\n";
    }
    if (scalar(@g_constants) > 0) {
        $src = $src . "\n";
    }

    # Package-level declarations of `our` variables from earlier evals
    foreach my str $our_decl (@g_our_decls) {
        $src = $src . $our_decl . "\n";
    }
    if (scalar(@g_our_decls) > 0) {
        $src = $src . "\n";
    }

    # User-defined functions
    foreach my str $fndef (@g_functions) {
        $src = $src . $fndef . "\n\n";
    }

    my int $use_closure_wrap = (index($input, "__C__") < 0) ? 1 : 0;

    # Emit main eval function in the active target package; keep repl::repl_eval as entry point
    my str $eval_pkg = get_target_package();
    my str $eval_fn_name = ($eval_pkg eq "repl") ? "repl_eval" : "__jit_repl_eval";
    $src = $src . "package " . $eval_pkg . ";\n";
    $src = $src . "func " . $eval_fn_name . "() scalar {\n";

    # Declare tracked variables as real C `my` locals in repl_eval() and restore
    # previously-saved values from the global registry (unless redeclared in $input).
    my str $restore_code = "";
    # C names follow declaration order: the tracked declarations below come
    # first; a variable the input redeclares itself (non-closure path) is
    # declared later, in the user's code
    my hash %vk_first = ();
    my array @vk_order = jit_vk_ordered();
    foreach my str $ok (@vk_order) {
        my str $on = jit_vk_name($ok);
        my int $o_redecl = input_declares_var($input, $on, jit_vk_sigil($ok));
        if (!($use_closure_wrap == 0 && $o_redecl == 1) && !exists($vk_first{$on})) { $vk_first{$on} = $ok; }
    }
    foreach my str $ok (@vk_order) {
        my str $on = jit_vk_name($ok);
        if (!exists($vk_first{$on})) { $vk_first{$on} = $ok; }
    }
    my hash %vk_cname = ();
    foreach my str $vkey (@vk_order) {
        my str $vname = jit_vk_name($vkey);
        my str $type = $g_var_types{$vkey};
        my str $sigil = jit_vk_sigil($vkey);
        $vk_cname{$vkey} = jit_vk_cname($vkey, \%vk_first);

        my int $redecl = input_declares_var($input, $vname, $sigil);
        if ($use_closure_wrap == 0 && $redecl == 1) {
            next;
        }

        # Emit my TYPE SIGIL+name declaration with default value
        if ($type eq "array") {
            $src = $src . "    my array @" . $vname . " = ();\n";
        } elsif ($type eq "hash") {
            $src = $src . "    my hash %" . $vname . " = ();\n";
        } elsif ($type eq "int") {
            $src = $src . "    my int \$" . $vname . " = 0;\n";
        } elsif ($type eq "num") {
            $src = $src . "    my num \$" . $vname . " = 0.0;\n";
        } elsif ($type eq "str") {
            $src = $src . "    my str \$" . $vname . " = \"\";\n";
        } else {
            $src = $src . "    my scalar \$" . $vname . " = undef;\n";
        }

        # A redeclaration of the same type still restores: the new `my` is not
        # in scope in its own initializer, so `my $n = $n * 2` reads the
        # previous $n (Perl; V5-15). A type change starts fresh.
        my int $restore = ($redecl == 0) ? 1 : 0;
        if ($redecl == 1 && exists($g_prev_var_types{$vkey}) && $g_prev_var_types{$vkey} eq $type) {
            $restore = 1;
        }
        if ($restore == 1) {
            my str $cname = $vk_cname{$vkey};
            my str $rkey = jit_vk_reg($vkey);
            $restore_code = $restore_code . "        if (strada_global_exists(strada_new_str(\"" . $rkey . "\"))) {\n";
            $restore_code = $restore_code . "            StradaValue *__saved_" . $cname . " = strada_global_get_cstr(\"" . $rkey . "\");\n";
            $restore_code = $restore_code . "            strada_decref(" . $cname . ");\n";
            $restore_code = $restore_code . "            " . $cname . " = __saved_" . $cname . ";\n";
            $restore_code = $restore_code . "        }\n";
        }
    }

    # Emit restore __C__ block if we have variables to restore
    if ($restore_code ne "") {
        $src = $src . "    __C__ {\n";
        $src = $src . $restore_code;
        $src = $src . "    }\n\n";
    }

    $src = $src . "    # User code\n";

    my str $body_input = ($use_closure_wrap == 1) ? strip_toplevel_my($input) : $input;
    my str $tail = $body_input;
    my int $split_at = last_toplevel_semi($body_input);
    my str $prefix_stmts = "";
    if ($split_at >= 0) {
        $prefix_stmts = substr($body_input, 0, $split_at + 1);
        $tail = substr($body_input, $split_at + 1, length($body_input) - $split_at - 1);
    }

    my int $blk_end = leading_block_stmt_end($tail);
    while ($blk_end >= 0) {
        my str $blk_part = substr($tail, 0, $blk_end + 1);
        if ($prefix_stmts eq "") {
            $prefix_stmts = $blk_part;
        } else {
            $prefix_stmts = $prefix_stmts . "\n" . $blk_part;
        }
        $tail = substr($tail, $blk_end + 1, length($tail) - $blk_end - 1);
        $blk_end = leading_block_stmt_end($tail);
    }

    my str $trimmed = jit_strip_leading_ws_comments($tail);

    # Check if this is a standalone void function call (not part of a larger expression like my_void() // 42)
    my int $is_void_call = 0;
    if ($trimmed =~ /^(say|print|warn|die|push|unshift|exit)\(/) {
        my int $op_pos = index($trimmed, "(");
        if ($op_pos >= 0 && jit_is_complete_call($trimmed, $op_pos) == 1) {
            $is_void_call = 1;
        }
    }
    foreach my str $fndef (@g_functions) {
        if ($fndef =~ /\)\s*void\s*\{/) {
            my str $vfn_name = get_function_name($fndef);
            if ($vfn_name ne "") {
                my int $cpos = rindex($vfn_name, "::");
                my str $bare_fn = ($cpos >= 0) ? substr($vfn_name, $cpos + 2, length($vfn_name) - $cpos - 2) : $vfn_name;
                my str $qprefix = $vfn_name . "(";
                my str $bprefix = $bare_fn . "(";
                if (length($trimmed) >= length($qprefix) && substr($trimmed, 0, length($qprefix)) eq $qprefix) {
                    if (jit_is_complete_call($trimmed, length($qprefix) - 1) == 1) {
                        $is_void_call = 1;
                    }
                } elsif (length($trimmed) >= length($bprefix) && substr($trimmed, 0, length($bprefix)) eq $bprefix) {
                    if (jit_is_complete_call($trimmed, length($bprefix) - 1) == 1) {
                        $is_void_call = 1;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    my int $is_return_stmt = 0;
    if ($trimmed =~ /^return(\s|;|\(|$)/) { $is_return_stmt = 1; }

    # Check if this is a statement (not an expression to capture)
    my int $is_statement = 0;
    if ($trimmed =~ /^my\s+/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^our\s+/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^const\s+/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^local\s+/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^if\s*\(/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^unless\s/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^while\s*\(/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^until\s*\(/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^do\s*\{/) {
        my int $ob_pos = index($trimmed, "{");
        if ($ob_pos >= 0) {
            my int $cb_pos = jit_find_matching($trimmed, $ob_pos, "{", "}");
            if ($cb_pos >= 0 && substr($trimmed, $cb_pos + 1, length($trimmed) - $cb_pos - 1) =~ /^\s*while\s*\(/) {
                $is_statement = 1;
            }
        }
    }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^for\s/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^foreach\s/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^switch\s*\(/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^try\s*\{/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^throw(\s|;|\(|$)/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^goto\s+/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^\{/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^[\$\@\%]\w+\s*([+\-*\/%.]?=|&&=|\|\|=|\/\/=)[^=~]/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^[\$\@\%]\w+\s*=$/) { $is_statement = 1; }
    if ($trimmed =~ /^\([^)]+\)\s*=[^=~]/) { $is_statement = 1; }

    my str $last_char = "";
    if (length($trimmed) > 0) {
        $last_char = substr($trimmed, length($trimmed) - 1, 1);
    }

    if ($use_closure_wrap == 1) {
        # Wrap user body in a helper closure so even an explicit `return EXPR;`
        # returns to repl_eval(), which then saves live *__repl_caps[i] cells!
        my array @tracked_names = jit_vk_ordered();
        my int $tracked_count = scalar(@tracked_names);
        $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__repl_fn = func() scalar {\n";
        if ($tracked_count > 0) {
            $src = $src . "        if (0) {\n";
            my int $ti = 0;
            while ($ti < $tracked_count) {
                my str $tvk = $tracked_names[$ti];
                my str $tvn = jit_vk_name($tvk);
                my str $tvt = $g_var_types{$tvk};
                if ($tvt eq "array") {
                    $src = $src . "            my scalar \$__touch_" . $ti . " = \\@" . $tvn . ";\n";
                } elsif ($tvt eq "hash") {
                    $src = $src . "            my scalar \$__touch_" . $ti . " = \\%" . $tvn . ";\n";
                } else {
                    $src = $src . "            my scalar \$__touch_" . $ti . " = \$" . $tvn . ";\n";
                }
                $ti = $ti + 1;
            }
            $src = $src . "        }\n";
            $src = $src . "        __C__ { __repl_caps = __captures; }\n";
        }
        if ($prefix_stmts ne "") {
            $src = $src . "        " . $prefix_stmts . "\n";
        }
        if ($is_return_stmt == 1) {
            my str $code_line = $tail;
            if ($last_char ne ";") { $code_line = $tail . "\n;"; }
            $src = $src . "        " . $code_line . "\n";
            $src = $src . "        return undef;\n";
        } elsif ($is_statement == 1) {
            my str $code_line = $tail;
            if ($last_char ne ";" && $last_char ne "}") {
                $code_line = $tail . "\n;";
            }
            $src = $src . "        " . $code_line . "\n";
            $src = $src . "        return undef;\n";
        } elsif ($is_void_call == 1) {
            my str $code_line = $tail;
            if ($last_char ne ";") { $code_line = $tail . "\n;"; }
            $src = $src . "        " . $code_line . "\n";
            $src = $src . "        return undef;\n";
        } else {
            my str $expr = $trimmed;
            if ($last_char eq ";") {
                $expr = substr($trimmed, 0, length($trimmed) - 1);
            }
            if ($expr eq "") {
                $src = $src . "        return undef;\n";
            } else {
                $src = $src . "        return " . $expr . "\n;\n";
            }
        }
        $src = $src . "    };\n";
        if ($tracked_count > 0) {
            my str $persist_caps = "        __C__ {\n"
                . "            if (__repl_caps) {\n";
            my int $si = 0;
            while ($si < $tracked_count) {
                my str $svn = $tracked_names[$si];
                $persist_caps = $persist_caps
                    . "                if (*__repl_caps[" . $si . "]) {\n"
                    . "                    strada_incref(*__repl_caps[" . $si . "]);\n"
                    . "                    strada_global_set_cstr(\"" . jit_vk_reg($svn) . "\", *__repl_caps[" . $si . "]);\n"
                    . "                }\n";
                $si = $si + 1;
            }
            $persist_caps = $persist_caps
                . "            }\n"
                . "            __repl_caps = (__repl_caps_sp > 0) ? __repl_caps_stack[--__repl_caps_sp] : NULL;\n"
                . "            if (__repl_caps_sp == 0 && __repl_caps_stack != NULL) {\n"
                . "                free(__repl_caps_stack);\n"
                . "                __repl_caps_stack = NULL;\n"
                . "                __repl_caps_cap = 0;\n"
                . "            }\n"
                . "        }\n";
            $src = $src . "    __C__ {\n"
                . "        if (__repl_caps_sp >= __repl_caps_cap) {\n"
                . "            int ncap = (__repl_caps_cap == 0) ? 64 : (__repl_caps_cap * 2);\n"
                . "            StradaValue ****ns = (StradaValue ****)realloc(__repl_caps_stack, (size_t)ncap * sizeof(StradaValue ***));\n"
                . "            if (ns) {\n"
                . "                __repl_caps_stack = ns;\n"
                . "                __repl_caps_cap = ncap;\n"
                . "            }\n"
                . "        }\n"
                . "        if (__repl_caps_sp < __repl_caps_cap) { __repl_caps_stack[__repl_caps_sp++] = __repl_caps; }\n"
                . "        __repl_caps = NULL;\n"
                . "    }\n";
            $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = undef;\n";
            $src = $src . "    try {\n";
            $src = $src . "        \$__result = \$__repl_fn->();\n";
            $src = $src . "    } catch (\$__jit_e) {\n";
            $src = $src . $persist_caps;
            $src = $src . "        throw \$__jit_e;\n";
            $src = $src . "    }\n";
            $src = $src . $persist_caps;
        } else {
            $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = \$__repl_fn->();\n";
        }
    } else {
        if ($prefix_stmts ne "") {
            $src = $src . "    " . $prefix_stmts . "\n";
        }
        if ($is_return_stmt == 1) {
            my str $ret_expr = substr($trimmed, 6, length($trimmed) - 6);
            $ret_expr =~ s/^\s+//;
            $ret_expr =~ s/\s+$//;
            if (length($ret_expr) > 0 && substr($ret_expr, length($ret_expr) - 1, 1) eq ";") {
                $ret_expr = substr($ret_expr, 0, length($ret_expr) - 1);
                $ret_expr =~ s/\s+$//;
            }
            if ($ret_expr eq "") {
                $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = undef;\n";
            } else {
                $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = " . $ret_expr . "\n;\n";
            }
        } elsif ($is_statement == 1) {
            my str $code_line = $tail;
            if ($last_char ne ";" && $last_char ne "}") {
                $code_line = $tail . "\n;";
            }
            $src = $src . "    " . $code_line . "\n";
            $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = undef;\n";
        } elsif ($is_void_call == 1) {
            my str $code_line = $tail;
            if ($last_char ne ";") { $code_line = $tail . "\n;"; }
            $src = $src . "    " . $code_line . "\n";
            $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = undef;\n";
        } else {
            my str $expr = $trimmed;
            if ($last_char eq ";") {
                $expr = substr($trimmed, 0, length($trimmed) - 1);
            }
            if ($expr eq "") {
                $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = undef;\n";
            } else {
                $src = $src . "    my scalar \$__result = " . $expr . "\n;\n";
            }
        }

        # Save all tracked variables back to global registry (inline __C__ path)
        my str $save_c = "";
        foreach my str $svk (jit_vk_ordered()) {
            my str $cv = $vk_cname{$svk};
            $save_c = $save_c . "        strada_incref(" . $cv . ");\n";
            $save_c = $save_c . "        strada_global_set_cstr(\"" . jit_vk_reg($svk) . "\", " . $cv . ");\n";
        }
        if ($save_c ne "") {
            $src = $src . "\n    __C__ {\n";
            $src = $src . $save_c;
            $src = $src . "    }\n";
        }
    }

    $src = $src . "\n    return \$__result;\n";
    $src = $src . "}\n";
    if ($eval_pkg ne "repl") {
        $src = $src . "\npackage repl;\nfunc repl_eval() scalar {\n    return " . $eval_pkg . "::__jit_repl_eval();\n}\n";
    }

    return $src;
}

# Create a private 0700 temp directory if we don't have one yet
private func ensure_private_tmpdir() void {
    if ($g_tmpdir_owned == 1 && length($g_tmpdir) > 0 && core::is_dir($g_tmpdir) == 1) {
        return;
    }
    my str $d = core::mkdtemp("/tmp/strada_jit_XXXXXX");
    if (length($d) == 0) {
        throw "Strada::JIT: Could not create private temp directory";
    }
    $g_tmpdir = $d;
    $g_tmpdir_owned = 1;
}

private func snapshot_var_types() scalar {
    my hash %copy = ();
    foreach my str $k (keys(%g_var_types)) {
        $copy{$k} = $g_var_types{$k};
    }
    return \%copy;
}

private func restore_var_types(scalar $saved) void {
    %g_var_types = ();
    if (defined($saved)) {
        foreach my str $k (keys(%{$saved})) {
            $g_var_types{$k} = $saved->{$k};
        }
    }
}

# Compile and execute a single eval, returns result
private func eval_one(str $input) scalar {
    ensure_private_tmpdir();
    $g_eval_count = $g_eval_count + 1;

    my str $base = $g_tmpdir . "/strada_repl_lib_" . $g_eval_count;
    my str $src_file = $base . ".strada";
    my str $c_file = $base . ".c";
    my str $so_file = $base . ".so";

    # Register any new variables (snapshot for rollback if compilation/load fails)
    my scalar $saved_vtypes = snapshot_var_types();
    %g_prev_var_types = %{$saved_vtypes};
    register_variables($input);
    register_our_decls($input);

    # Generate Strada source
    my str $strada_src = generate_source($input);

    if ($g_debug == 1) {
        say("[JIT DEBUG] Generated source:");
        say($strada_src);
    }

    # Write source file
    my scalar $fh = core::open($src_file, "w");
    if (!defined($fh)) {
        restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
        throw "JIT: Could not create temp file: " . $src_file;
    }
    core::fwrite($fh, $strada_src);
    core::close($fh);

    # Step 1: stradac → C
    my str $stradac_cmd = shell_quote($g_stradac_path) . " ";
    foreach my str $lp (@g_lib_paths) {
        $stradac_cmd = $stradac_cmd . "-L " . shell_quote($lp) . " ";
    }
    $stradac_cmd = $stradac_cmd . shell_quote($src_file) . " " . shell_quote($c_file) . " 2>&1";
    my scalar $pipe = core::popen($stradac_cmd, "r");
    my str $compile_output = "";
    if (defined($pipe)) {
        my scalar $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
        while (defined($line)) {
            $compile_output = $compile_output . $line;
            $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
        }
        core::pclose($pipe);
    }

    if (core::is_file($c_file) == 0) {
        # Clean up
        core::unlink($src_file);
        restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
        # Extract useful error message
        my str $err_msg = $compile_output;
        $err_msg =~ s/^Strada Compiler[^\n]*\n//;
        $err_msg =~ s/^Compiling:[^\n]*\n//;
        $err_msg =~ s/^\s+//;
        $err_msg =~ s/\s+$//;
        throw "JIT compile error: " . $err_msg;
    }

    if ($g_cdebug == 1) {
        say("[JIT CDEBUG] Generated C: " . $c_file);
        my scalar $cfh = core::open($c_file, "r");
        if (defined($cfh)) {
            my str $cline = <$cfh>;
            while (defined($cline)) {
                print($cline);
                $cline = <$cfh>;
            }
            core::close($cfh);
        }
    }

    my scalar $result = undef;
    my int $tcc_init_fn = 0;

    # Step 2: C → .so
    if ($g_compiler eq "tcc") {
        if ($g_runtime_path eq "") {
            core::unlink($src_file);
            core::unlink($c_file);
            restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
            throw "JIT: Could not find Strada runtime files for tcc backend";
        }

        my str $c_content = core::slurp($c_file);
        my str $hdr_line = "#include \"strada_runtime.h\"\n";
        my str $tcc_line = "#include \"strada_runtime_tcc.h\"\n";
        if (length($c_content) >= length($hdr_line) && substr($c_content, 0, length($hdr_line)) eq $hdr_line) {
            $c_content = $tcc_line . substr($c_content, length($hdr_line), length($c_content) - length($hdr_line));
        } else {
            my int $hpos = index($c_content, "\n" . $hdr_line);
            if ($hpos >= 0) {
                my int $after_h = $hpos + 1 + length($hdr_line);
                $c_content = substr($c_content, 0, $hpos + 1) . $tcc_line
                    . substr($c_content, $after_h, length($c_content) - $after_h);
            }
        }
        # tcc silently drops __attribute__((constructor)), so the .so's
        # __strada_init_globals (OOP method/inherit registration, globals)
        # would never run (V5-10): export it and call it after dlopen.
        my str $ctor_decl = "__attribute__((constructor))\nstatic void __strada_init_globals(void) {";
        my int $cpos = index($c_content, $ctor_decl);
        if ($cpos >= 0) {
            $c_content = substr($c_content, 0, $cpos) . "void __strada_init_globals(void) {"
                . substr($c_content, $cpos + length($ctor_decl), length($c_content) - $cpos - length($ctor_decl));
            $tcc_init_fn = 1;
        }
        core::spew($c_file, $c_content);

        my str $tcc_cmd = "tcc -shared -o " . shell_quote($so_file) . " " . shell_quote($c_file) . " -I" . shell_quote($g_runtime_path) . " -ldl -lm -lpthread 2>&1";
        $pipe = core::popen($tcc_cmd, "r");
        my str $tcc_output = "";
        if (defined($pipe)) {
            my scalar $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
            while (defined($line)) {
                $tcc_output = $tcc_output . $line;
                $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
            }
            core::pclose($pipe);
        }

        if (core::is_file($so_file) == 0) {
            core::unlink($src_file);
            core::unlink($c_file);
            restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
            throw "JIT C compile error (tcc): " . $tcc_output;
        }
    } else {
        # gcc via the strada wrapper.
        # -O0 explicitly: snippets are one-shot (dlopen'd, executed, discarded),
        # so any -O2 + LTO time is pure overhead. -O0 also triggers strada's
        # speed flags (-pipe, -fno-var-tracking, etc).
        my str $lib_flags = "";
        foreach my str $lp (@g_lib_paths) {
            $lib_flags = $lib_flags . " -L " . shell_quote($lp);
        }
        my str $strada_bin = "";
        if ($g_stradac_path ne "" && $g_stradac_path ne "stradac") {
            my str $cand = core::dirname($g_stradac_path) . "/strada";
            if (core::is_file($cand) == 1) {
                $strada_bin = $cand;
            }
        }
        if ($strada_bin eq "") {
            $strada_bin = "strada";
        }
        my str $gcc_cmd = shell_quote($strada_bin) . " -O0 --shared" . $lib_flags . " " . shell_quote($src_file) . " -o " . shell_quote($so_file) . " 2>&1";
        $pipe = core::popen($gcc_cmd, "r");
        my str $output = "";
        if (defined($pipe)) {
            my scalar $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
            while (defined($line)) {
                $output = $output . $line;
                $line = core::fgets($pipe, 4096);
            }
            core::pclose($pipe);
        }

        if (core::is_file($so_file) == 0) {
            core::unlink($src_file);
            if (core::is_file($c_file) == 1) {
                core::unlink($c_file);
            }
            restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
            throw "JIT C compile error (gcc): " . $output;
        }
    }

    # Step 3: Load and execute
    my array @mod_pkgs = keys(%g_oop_packages);
    my int $mpi = 0;
    my int $mp_count = scalar(@mod_pkgs);
    if ($mp_count > 0) {
        $g_did_oop_reset = 1;
    }
    while ($mpi < $mp_count) {
        my str $mpkg = $mod_pkgs[$mpi];
        __C__ {
            char *p = strada_to_str(mpkg);
            if (p) {
                strada_oop_reset_package(p);
                free(p);
            }
        }
        $mpi = $mpi + 1;
    }

    my int $lib = core::dl_open($so_file);
    if ($lib == 0) {
        my str $dl_err = core::dl_error();
        core::unlink($src_file);
        if (core::is_file($c_file) == 1) {
            core::unlink($c_file);
        }
        core::unlink($so_file);
        restore_var_types($saved_vtypes);
        throw "JIT: Could not load compiled library: " . $dl_err;
    }

    # Keep handle tracked and unlink temp files immediately (unlinking an open .so keeps its mapping alive)
    push(@g_open_libs, $lib);
    core::unlink($src_file);
    if (core::is_file($c_file) == 1) {
        core::unlink($c_file);
    }
    if (core::is_file($so_file) == 1) {
        core::unlink($so_file);
    }

    if ($tcc_init_fn == 1) {
        my int $init_fn = core::dl_sym($lib, "__strada_init_globals");
        if ($init_fn != 0) {
            __C__ {
                void (*jit_init_p)(void) = (void (*)(void))(intptr_t)strada_to_int(init_fn);
                if (jit_init_p) jit_init_p();
            }
        }
    }

    my int $fn = core::dl_sym($lib, "repl_eval");
    if ($fn != 0) {
        $result = core::dl_call_sv($fn, undef);
    }

    return $result;
}

# ============================================================
# Public API
# ============================================================

# Initialize the JIT engine
# $compiler_pref: optional compiler preference ("tcc" or "gcc"), empty for auto-detect
func init(str ...@args) void {
    my str $compiler_pref = "";
    if (scalar(@args) > 0) {
        $compiler_pref = $args[0];
    }

    $g_stradac_path = detect_stradac();
    if ($g_stradac_path eq "") {
        throw "Strada::JIT::init: Could not find stradac compiler. Make sure stradac is in your PATH or run from the Strada directory.";
    }

    $g_runtime_path = detect_runtime();

    if ($compiler_pref ne "") {
        my int $available = 0;
        if ($compiler_pref eq "tcc") {
            __C__ {
                available = strada_new_int(repl_command_exists("tcc"));
            }
        } elsif ($compiler_pref eq "gcc") {
            __C__ {
                available = strada_new_int(repl_command_exists("gcc"));
            }
        } else {
            throw "Strada::JIT::init: Unknown compiler: " . $compiler_pref . " (valid: tcc, gcc)";
        }
        if ($available == 0) {
            throw "Strada::JIT::init: Compiler not available: " . $compiler_pref;
        }
        $g_compiler = $compiler_pref;
    } else {
        $g_compiler = detect_compiler();
        if ($g_compiler eq "") {
            throw "Strada::JIT::init: No C compiler found (need tcc or gcc)";
        }
    }

    ensure_private_tmpdir();
    $g_initialized = 1;
}

# Evaluate Strada code and return the result
private func upsert_constant(str $key, str $entry) void {
    if ($key ne "" && exists($g_constant_idx{$key})) {
        $g_constants[$g_constant_idx{$key}] = $entry;
        return;
    }
    if ($key ne "") {
        $g_constant_idx{$key} = scalar(@g_constants);
    }
    push(@g_constants, $entry);
}

private func snapshot_jit_state() scalar {
    my hash %vt = ();
    my array @vt_keys = keys(%g_var_types);
    my int $vi = 0;
    while ($vi < scalar(@vt_keys)) {
        my str $k = $vt_keys[$vi];
        $vt{$k} = $g_var_types{$k};
        $vi = $vi + 1;
    }

    my array @imp = ();
    my int $ii = 0;
    while ($ii < scalar(@g_imports)) {
        push(@imp, $g_imports[$ii]);
        $ii = $ii + 1;
    }

    my array @consts = ();
    my int $ci = 0;
    while ($ci < scalar(@g_constants)) {
        push(@consts, $g_constants[$ci]);
        $ci = $ci + 1;
    }

    my hash %cidx = ();
    my array @c_keys = keys(%g_constant_idx);
    my int $cki = 0;
    while ($cki < scalar(@c_keys)) {
        my str $ck = $c_keys[$cki];
        $cidx{$ck} = $g_constant_idx{$ck};
        $cki = $cki + 1;
    }

    my array @funcs = ();
    my int $fi = 0;
    while ($fi < scalar(@g_functions)) {
        push(@funcs, $g_functions[$fi]);
        $fi = $fi + 1;
    }

    my hash %oops = ();
    my array @op_keys = keys(%g_oop_packages);
    my int $oi = 0;
    while ($oi < scalar(@op_keys)) {
        my str $op = $op_keys[$oi];
        $oops{$op} = $g_oop_packages{$op};
        $oi = $oi + 1;
    }

    my hash %snap = ();
    $snap{"var_types"} = \%vt;
    $snap{"imports"} = \@imp;
    $snap{"constants"} = \@consts;
    $snap{"constant_idx"} = \%cidx;
    $snap{"functions"} = \@funcs;
    $snap{"oop_packages"} = \%oops;
    $snap{"current_package"} = $g_current_package;
    my array @ourd = ();
    foreach my str $od (@g_our_decls) { push(@ourd, $od); }
    $snap{"our_decls"} = \@ourd;
    return \%snap;
}

private func restore_jit_state(scalar $snap) void {
    my scalar $vt = $snap->{"var_types"};
    my scalar $vt_keys = [keys($vt)];
    my scalar $imp = $snap->{"imports"};
    my scalar $consts = $snap->{"constants"};
    my scalar $cidx = $snap->{"constant_idx"};
    my scalar $c_keys = [keys($cidx)];
    my scalar $funcs = $snap->{"functions"};
    my scalar $oops = $snap->{"oop_packages"};
    my scalar $op_keys = [keys($oops)];
    my array @cur_vt_keys = keys(%g_var_types);
    my array @cur_op_keys = keys(%g_oop_packages);

    # Clear global hashes/arrays before loops (avoids parser % modulo ambiguity)
    %g_var_types = ();
    %g_constant_idx = ();
    %g_oop_packages = ();
    @g_imports = ();
    @g_constants = ();
    @g_functions = ();

    my int $cvi = 0;
    while ($cvi < scalar(@cur_vt_keys)) {
        my str $cvk = $cur_vt_keys[$cvi];
        if (!exists($vt->{$cvk})) {
            core::global_delete(jit_vk_reg($cvk));
        }
        $cvi = $cvi + 1;
    }
    my int $copi = 0;
    while ($copi < scalar(@cur_op_keys)) {
        my str $cpk = $cur_op_keys[$copi];
        if (!exists($oops->{$cpk})) {
            __C__ {
                char *p = strada_to_str(cpk);
                if (p) {
                    strada_oop_reset_package(p);
                    free(p);
                }
            }
        }
        $copi = $copi + 1;
    }

    my int $vi = 0;
    while ($vi < size($vt_keys)) {
        my str $k = $vt_keys->[$vi];
        $g_var_types{$k} = $vt->{$k};
        $vi = $vi + 1;
    }
    my int $ii = 0;
    while ($ii < size($imp)) {
        push(@g_imports, $imp->[$ii]);
        $ii = $ii + 1;
    }
    my int $ci = 0;
    while ($ci < size($consts)) {
        push(@g_constants, $consts->[$ci]);
        $ci = $ci + 1;
    }
    my int $cki = 0;
    while ($cki < size($c_keys)) {
        my str $ck = $c_keys->[$cki];
        $g_constant_idx{$ck} = $cidx->{$ck};
        $cki = $cki + 1;
    }
    my int $fi = 0;
    while ($fi < size($funcs)) {
        push(@g_functions, $funcs->[$fi]);
        $fi = $fi + 1;
    }
    my int $oi = 0;
    while ($oi < size($op_keys)) {
        my str $op = $op_keys->[$oi];
        $g_oop_packages{$op} = $oops->{$op};
        $oi = $oi + 1;
    }
    $g_current_package = $snap->{"current_package"};
    # our declarations: drop the ones this failed eval added
    my scalar $sod = $snap->{"our_decls"};
    my int $keep = defined($sod) ? size($sod) : 0;
    while (scalar(@g_our_decls) > $keep) {
        pop(@g_our_decls);
    }
    my array @odk = keys(%g_our_decl_idx);
    foreach my str $ok (@odk) {
        if ($g_our_decl_idx{$ok} >= $keep) {
            delete($g_our_decl_idx{$ok});
        } else {
            $g_our_decls[$g_our_decl_idx{$ok}] = $sod->[$g_our_decl_idx{$ok}];
        }
    }
}

private func jit_strip_leading_ws_comments(str $s) str {
    my str $cur = $s;
    while (length($cur) > 0) {
        my str $before = $cur;
        $cur =~ s/^\s+//;
        if ($cur =~ /^#/) {
            $cur =~ s/^#[^\n]*(?:\n|$)//;
        } elsif (length($cur) >= 2 && substr($cur, 0, 2) eq "/*") {
            my str $rest = substr($cur, 2, length($cur) - 2);
            my int $end_cmt = index($rest, "*/");
            if ($end_cmt >= 0) {
                $cur = substr($rest, $end_cmt + 2, length($rest) - $end_cmt - 2);
            } else {
                last;
            }
        }
        if ($cur eq $before) {
            last;
        }
    }
    $cur =~ s/\s+$//;
    return $cur;
}

private func eval_inner(str $code, scalar $flags) scalar {
    my str $input = jit_strip_leading_ws_comments($code);

    if ($input eq "") {
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for import statement (split trailing remainder after ';' if present)
    if (is_import($input)) {
        my int $semi = first_toplevel_semi($input);
        if ($semi >= 0) {
            my str $stmt = substr($input, 0, $semi + 1);
            my str $rem = substr($input, $semi + 1, length($input) - $semi - 1);
            $rem =~ s/^\s+//;
            $rem =~ s/\s+$//;
            register_import($stmt);
            $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
            if ($rem ne "") {
                return eval_inner($rem, $flags);
            }
            return undef;
        }
        register_import($input);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for package declaration (split trailing remainder after ';' if present)
    if (is_package_decl($input)) {
        my int $semi = first_toplevel_semi($input);
        my str $pkg_stmt = $input;
        my str $rem = "";
        if ($semi >= 0) {
            $pkg_stmt = substr($input, 0, $semi);
            $rem = substr($input, $semi + 1, length($input) - $semi - 1);
            $rem =~ s/^\s+//;
            $rem =~ s/\s+$//;
        }
        my str $pkg_name = $pkg_stmt;
        $pkg_name =~ s/^\s*package\s+//;
        $pkg_name =~ s/\s*;.*$//;
        $pkg_name =~ s/\s+$//;
        $g_current_package = $pkg_name;
        delete($flags, "extends_seen_" . $pkg_name);
        if ($rem ne "") {
            return eval_inner($rem, $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for const declaration (split trailing remainder if present)
    if ($input =~ /^\s*const\s+/) {
        my int $semi = first_toplevel_semi($input);
        my str $const_line = $input;
        my str $rem = "";
        if ($semi >= 0) {
            $const_line = substr($input, 0, $semi + 1);
            $rem = substr($input, $semi + 1, length($input) - $semi - 1);
            $rem =~ s/^\s+//;
            $rem =~ s/\s+$//;
        } else {
            $const_line =~ s/\s+$//;
            if (substr($const_line, length($const_line) - 1, 1) ne ";") {
                $const_line = $const_line . "\n;";
            }
        }
        my str $tpkg = get_target_package();
        my str $entry = "package " . $tpkg . ";\n" . $const_line;
        my str $ckey = "";
        if ($const_line =~ /^\s*const\s+(?:(?:int|num|str|scalar|array|hash)\s+)?([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/) {
            $ckey = $tpkg . "::const::" . $1;
        }
        upsert_constant($ckey, $entry);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
        if ($rem ne "") {
            return eval_inner($rem, $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for enum declaration
    if ($input =~ /^\s*enum\s+/) {
        my array @eparts = extract_function_def($input);
        my str $enum_line = $eparts[0];
        $enum_line =~ s/\s+$//;
        if (substr($enum_line, length($enum_line) - 1, 1) ne "}") {
            if (substr($enum_line, length($enum_line) - 1, 1) ne ";") {
                $enum_line = $enum_line . ";";
            }
        }
        my str $tpkg = get_target_package();
        my str $entry = "package " . $tpkg . ";\n" . $enum_line;
        my str $ekey = "";
        if ($enum_line =~ /^\s*enum\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*)/) {
            $ekey = $tpkg . "::enum::" . $1;
        }
        upsert_constant($ekey, $entry);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
        if ($eparts[1] ne "") {
            return eval_inner($eparts[1], $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for OOP package-level statements (has, extends, use overload)
    if (is_oop_decl($input)) {
        my int $semi = first_toplevel_semi($input);
        my str $oop_stmt = $input;
        my str $rem = "";
        if ($semi >= 0) {
            $oop_stmt = substr($input, 0, $semi + 1);
            $rem = substr($input, $semi + 1, length($input) - $semi - 1);
            $rem =~ s/^\s+//;
            $rem =~ s/\s+$//;
        } else {
            $oop_stmt =~ s/\s+$//;
            if (substr($oop_stmt, length($oop_stmt) - 1, 1) ne ";") {
                $oop_stmt = $oop_stmt . "\n;";
            }
        }
        my str $tpkg = get_target_package();
        track_oop_package($tpkg);
        my str $entry = "package " . $tpkg . ";\n" . $oop_stmt;
        my str $okey = "";
        if ($oop_stmt =~ /^\s*has\s+.*?[\$@%]([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/) {
            $okey = $tpkg . "::has::" . $1;
        } elsif ($oop_stmt =~ /^\s*(?:extends|inherit)\s+([\s\S]*)$/) {
            $okey = $tpkg . "::extends";
            my str $eflag = "extends_seen_" . $tpkg;
            if (($flags->{$eflag} + 0) == 1 && exists($g_constant_idx{$okey})) {
                $g_constants[$g_constant_idx{$okey}] = $g_constants[$g_constant_idx{$okey}] . "\n" . $entry;
            } else {
                $flags->{$eflag} = 1;
                upsert_constant($okey, $entry);
            }
            $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
            if ($rem ne "") {
                return eval_inner($rem, $flags);
            }
            return undef;
        } elsif ($oop_stmt =~ /^\s*use\s+overload\b([\s\S]*)$/) {
            my str $ov = $1;
            $ov =~ s/^\s+//;
            $ov =~ s/[\s;]+$//;
            $ov =~ s/\s+/ /g;
            if ($ov =~ /^"((?:\\.|[^"\\])*)"\s*=>\s*[^,]+$/) {
                $okey = $tpkg . "::overload::\"" . $1 . "\"";
            } elsif ($ov =~ /^'((?:\\.|[^'\\])*)'\s*=>\s*[^,]+$/) {
                $okey = $tpkg . "::overload::'" . $1 . "'";
            } else {
                $okey = $tpkg . "::overload::" . $ov;
            }
        }
        upsert_constant($okey, $entry);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
        if ($rem ne "") {
            return eval_inner($rem, $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for method modifier (before/after/around)
    if (is_modifier_def($input)) {
        my array @mparts = extract_function_def($input);
        my str $tpkg = get_target_package();
        track_oop_package($tpkg);
        push(@g_functions, "package " . $tpkg . ";\n" . $mparts[0]);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
        if ($mparts[1] ne "") {
            return eval_inner($mparts[1], $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Check for function definition
    if (is_function_def($input)) {
        my array @parts = extract_function_def($input);
        register_function($parts[0]);
        $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;

        # If there's a remainder after the function def, evaluate it recursively
        if ($parts[1] ne "") {
            return eval_inner($parts[1], $flags);
        }
        return undef;
    }

    # Named functions after other statements (`my $x = 1; func f() {...} f()`)
    # are hoisted like Perl's compile-time subs (V5-13).
    my str $hoisted = jit_hoist_named_funcs($input, $flags);
    if ($hoisted ne $input) {
        return eval_inner($hoisted, $flags);
    }

    $flags->{"did_compile"} = 1;
    return eval_one($input);
}

# Remove the first top-level named `func`/`fn` definition that starts a
# statement (after `;` or a block's `}`), registering it; returns the input
# unchanged when there is none.
private func jit_hoist_named_funcs(str $input, scalar $flags) str {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    if ($g_strip_unclosed == 1 || length($cleaned) != length($input)) {
        return $input;
    }
    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    my int $depth = 0;
    my int $i = 0;
    my int $stmt_start = 1;
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);
        if ($c eq "{" || $c eq "(" || $c eq "[") {
            $depth = $depth + 1;
            $stmt_start = 0;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($c eq "}" || $c eq ")" || $c eq "]") {
            $depth = $depth - 1;
            $stmt_start = ($depth == 0 && $c eq "}") ? 1 : 0;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($depth == 0 && $c eq ";") {
            $stmt_start = 1;
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if (jit_is_ws($c) == 1) {
            $i = $i + 1;
            next;
        }
        if ($depth == 0 && $stmt_start == 1 && $i > 0) {
            my str $rest = substr($input, $i, length($input) - $i);
            if (is_function_def($rest) == 1) {
                my array @parts = extract_function_def($rest);
                register_function($parts[0]);
                $flags->{"added_decl"} = 1;
                my str $before = substr($input, 0, $i);
                $before =~ s/\s+$//;
                if ($parts[1] eq "") { return $before; }
                return $before . "\n" . $parts[1];
            }
        }
        $stmt_start = 0;
        $i = $i + 1;
    }
    return $input;
}

func eval(str $code) scalar {
    if ($g_initialized == 0) {
        throw "Strada::JIT::eval: Not initialized. Call Strada::JIT::init() first.";
    }

    my str $input = jit_strip_leading_ws_comments($code);

    if ($input eq "") {
        return undef;
    }

    my scalar $snap = snapshot_jit_state();
    my hash %flags = ();
    $flags{"did_compile"} = 0;
    $flags{"added_decl"} = 0;
    $g_did_oop_reset = 0;
    my scalar $res = undef;
    try {
        $res = eval_inner($input, \%flags);
        if ($flags{"did_compile"} == 0 && $flags{"added_decl"} == 1) {
            eval_one("undef");
        }
    } catch ($jit_err) {
        restore_jit_state($snap);
        if ($g_did_oop_reset == 1 && scalar(keys(%g_oop_packages)) > 0) {
            try {
                eval_one("undef");
            } catch ($__re) {}
        }
        $g_did_oop_reset = 0;
        throw $jit_err;
    }
    $g_did_oop_reset = 0;
    return $res;
}

# Compile a script file as a complete program in one shot and exec it.
# Returns the script's exit code (the rc from the compiled binary, or a
# non-zero compile-error code if stradac/cc fails).
#
# This is the whole-file counterpart to eval(): it avoids the per-statement
# compile overhead of the REPL-style chunked path by handing the whole file
# to stradac at once, then exec'ing the resulting executable. Intended for
# the `strada --script FILE` entry point.
#
# Reuses the `strada` driver script for the compile (so it benefits from
# PCRE2 / runtime path / optimization handling without duplicating logic).
func decode_wait_status(int $rc) int {
    if ($rc < 0) { return 127; }
    my int $es = core::exit_status($rc);
    if ($es >= 0) { return $es; }
    my int $sig = $rc & 127;
    if ($sig > 0 && $sig != 127) { return 128 + $sig; }
    return 1;
}

func run_file_argv(str $filename, scalar $script_args) int {
    if ($g_initialized == 0) {
        throw "Strada::JIT::run_file: Not initialized. Call init() first.";
    }
    ensure_private_tmpdir();
    if (core::is_file($filename) == 0) {
        throw "Strada::JIT::run_file: File not found: " . $filename;
    }

    # Locate the strada driver next to the stradac we already found.
    my str $strada_bin = "";
    if ($g_stradac_path ne "" && $g_stradac_path ne "stradac") {
        my str $cand = core::dirname($g_stradac_path) . "/strada";
        if (core::is_file($cand) == 1) {
            $strada_bin = $cand;
        }
    }
    if ($strada_bin eq "") {
        $strada_bin = "strada";  # fall back to PATH
    }

    my int $pid = core::getpid();
    my str $exe_file = $g_tmpdir . "/strada_script_" . $pid;

    # Compile via the driver — quote paths defensively in case they contain spaces.
    my str $lib_flags = "";
    foreach my str $lp (@g_lib_paths) {
        $lib_flags = $lib_flags . " -L " . shell_quote($lp);
    }
    my str $compile_cmd = shell_quote($strada_bin) . $lib_flags . " -o " . shell_quote($exe_file) . " " . shell_quote($filename);
    my int $rc = decode_wait_status(core::system($compile_cmd));
    if ($rc != 0 || core::is_file($exe_file) == 0) {
        if ($rc == 0) { $rc = 1; }
        return $rc;
    }

    # Exec and propagate the script's exit code.
    my str $run_cmd = shell_quote($exe_file);
    if (defined($script_args) && ref($script_args) eq "ARRAY") {
        foreach my str $sa (@$script_args) {
            $run_cmd = $run_cmd . " " . shell_quote($sa);
        }
    }
    $rc = decode_wait_status(core::system($run_cmd));
    core::unlink($exe_file);
    return $rc;
}

func run_file(str $filename) int {
    my array @empty = ();
    return run_file_argv($filename, \@empty);
}

# Get a variable value from the persistent state (global registry)
func get(str $name) scalar {
    return core::global_get(jit_vk_reg(jit_vk_lookup($name)));
}

# Set a variable value in the persistent state (global registry)
func set(str $name, scalar $value) void {
    my str $vk = jit_vk_lookup($name);
    core::global_set(jit_vk_reg($vk), $value);
    # Also register the type if not already known
    if (!exists($g_var_types{$vk})) {
        my str $sg = jit_vk_sigil($vk);
        my str $ty = "scalar";
        if ($sg eq "@") { $ty = "array"; }
        if ($sg eq "%") { $ty = "hash"; }
        $g_var_types{$vk} = $ty;
    }
}

# Add a library search path
func add_lib_path(str $path) void {
    foreach my str $existing (@g_lib_paths) {
        if ($existing eq $path) {
            return;
        }
    }
    push(@g_lib_paths, $path);
}

# Reset all state (variables, functions, imports)
func reset() void {
    # Delete all repl:: globals from the registry
    # NOTE: must iterate keys BEFORE clearing the hash (parser bug:
    # %hash = () after while/foreach block is mis-parsed as MOD operator)
    my array @var_names = keys(%g_var_types);
    # `our` variables of the session (registry keys PKG::name)
    my array @our_keys = keys(%g_our_decl_idx);
    foreach my str $ok (@our_keys) {
        if ($ok =~ /^(.*)::[\$\@\%]([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)$/) {
            core::global_delete($1 . "::" . $2);
        }
    }
    my int $vi = 0;
    my int $var_count = scalar(@var_names);
    my array @oop_pkgs = keys(%g_ever_oop_packages);
    my int $opi = 0;
    my int $oop_pkg_count = scalar(@oop_pkgs);

    # Clear state hashes/arrays first (before any loops)
    %g_var_types = ();
    %g_oop_packages = ();
    %g_ever_oop_packages = ();
    %g_constant_idx = ();
    @g_functions = ();
    @g_constants = ();
    @g_imports = ();
    $g_current_package = "";
    @g_our_decls = ();
    %g_our_decl_idx = ();
    # $g_eval_count keeps counting: a reused .so path could make dlopen hand
    # back a still-mapped (retired) library instead of the new one.

    # Now delete globals using the saved key list
    while ($vi < $var_count) {
        core::global_delete(jit_vk_reg($var_names[$vi]));
        $vi = $vi + 1;
    }

    # Collect cyclic closures before dlclosing their shared libraries
    core::gc_collect();

    # Close accumulated library handles and clean up .so files
    my array @libs_to_close = @g_open_libs;
    my array @files_to_delete = @g_so_files;
    @g_open_libs = ();
    @g_so_files = ();

    # Reset OOP metadata for JIT-loaded packages before dlclosing their .so mappings
    while ($opi < $oop_pkg_count) {
        my str $opkg = $oop_pkgs[$opi];
        __C__ {
            char *p = strada_to_str(opkg);
            if (p) {
                strada_oop_reset_package(p);
                free(p);
            }
        }
        $opi = $opi + 1;
    }

    # The libraries are NOT dlclose'd: closures (and blessed objects whose
    # methods live there) obtained from earlier evals may still be held by the
    # host, and calling one into an unmapped .so segfaulted (V5-12). The
    # mappings stay until exit; the files are already unlinked.
    my int $li = 0;
    my int $lib_count = scalar(@libs_to_close);
    while ($li < $lib_count) {
        push(@g_retired_libs, $libs_to_close[$li]);
        $li = $li + 1;
    }
    my int $fi = 0;
    my int $file_count = scalar(@files_to_delete);
    while ($fi < $file_count) {
        if (core::is_file($files_to_delete[$fi]) == 1) {
            core::unlink($files_to_delete[$fi]);
        }
        $fi = $fi + 1;
    }
    if ($g_tmpdir_owned == 1 && length($g_tmpdir) > 0 && $g_tmpdir ne "/tmp") {
        core::rmdir($g_tmpdir);
        $g_tmpdir = "/tmp";
        $g_tmpdir_owned = 0;
    }
}

# Enable/disable debug mode (shows generated source)
func debug(int $enabled) void {
    $g_debug = $enabled;
}

# Enable/disable C debug mode (shows generated C code)
func cdebug(int $enabled) void {
    $g_cdebug = $enabled;
}

# Get the detected compiler name
func compiler() str {
    return $g_compiler;
}

# Get variable names and types as a hash (name -> type)
func var_types() hash {
    my hash %pub = ();
    foreach my str $k (keys(%g_var_types)) { $pub{jit_vk_public($k)} = $g_var_types{$k}; }
    return %pub;
}

# Get accumulated function definitions as an array
func functions() array {
    return @g_functions;
}

# Get accumulated import statements as an array
func imports() array {
    return @g_imports;
}

# Get library search paths as an array
func lib_paths() array {
    return @g_lib_paths;
}

# Get/set current package name
func current_package() str {
    return $g_current_package;
}

func set_package(str $name) void {
    $g_current_package = $name;
}

# Get the state hash (for direct access by JIT tools)
# Fetches current values from the global registry
func state() hash {
    my hash %result = ();
    my array @var_names = keys(%g_var_types);
    my int $si = 0;
    my int $scount = scalar(@var_names);
    while ($si < $scount) {
        my str $vkey = $var_names[$si];
        my scalar $val = core::global_get(jit_vk_reg($vkey));
        $result{jit_vk_public($vkey)} = $val;
        $si = $si + 1;
    }
    return %result;
}

# Check if input is a function definition (public wrapper)
func check_function_def(str $input) int {
    return is_function_def($input);
}

# Check if input is an import statement (public wrapper)
func check_import(str $input) int {
    return is_import($input);
}

# Check if input is a package declaration (public wrapper)
func check_package_decl(str $input) int {
    return is_package_decl($input);
}

# Check if braces/parens/brackets are balanced
func is_balanced(str $input) int {
    my str $cleaned = strip_strings_and_comments($input);
    if ($g_strip_unclosed == 1) {
        return 0;
    }
    my int $braces = 0;
    my int $parens = 0;
    my int $brackets = 0;

    my int $len = length($cleaned);
    my int $i = 0;
    while ($i < $len) {
        my str $c = substr($cleaned, $i, 1);

        if ($c eq "{") { $braces = $braces + 1; }
        if ($c eq "}") { $braces = $braces - 1; }
        if ($c eq "(") { $parens = $parens + 1; }
        if ($c eq ")") { $parens = $parens - 1; }
        if ($c eq "[") { $brackets = $brackets + 1; }
        if ($c eq "]") { $brackets = $brackets - 1; }

        $i = $i + 1;
    }

    if ($braces < 0 || $parens < 0 || $brackets < 0) {
        return 1;
    }

    if ($braces == 0 && $parens == 0) {
        if (index($cleaned, "{") < 0) {
            my str $tclean = $cleaned;
            $tclean =~ s/^\s+//;
            if ($tclean =~ /^func\s+/ || $tclean =~ /^fn\s+/ || $tclean =~ /^async\s+/ || $tclean =~ /^private\s+/) {
                return 0;
            }
        }
    }

    if ($braces == 0 && $parens == 0 && $brackets == 0) {
        if (jit_ends_with_operator($cleaned) == 1) {
            return 0;
        }
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

# 1 when the (string/comment-stripped) input ends in a binary operator, so
# the statement continues on the next line: `my $s = "a" .` (V5-17).
private func jit_ends_with_operator(str $cleaned) int {
    my str $t = $cleaned;
    $t =~ s/\s+$//;
    my int $n = length($t);
    if ($n == 0) { return 0; }
    if ($n >= 2) {
        my str $l2 = substr($t, $n - 2, 2);
        if ($l2 eq "++" || $l2 eq "--") { return 0; }
        if ($l2 eq "->" || $l2 eq "=>" || $l2 eq "::") { return 1; }
    }
    my str $lc = substr($t, $n - 1, 1);
    if ($lc eq ">") {
        # <STDIN> / <$fh> readline is a complete term
        if ($t =~ /<\$?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*>$/) { return 0; }
        return 1;
    }
    if (index(".+-*/%=,<&|!?:~^\\", $lc) >= 0) {
        return 1;
    }
    if ($t =~ /(?:^|[^\$\@\%\&A-Za-z0-9_:>])(and|or|not|xor|x|eq|ne|lt|gt|le|ge|cmp)$/) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}

END {
    Strada::JIT::reset();
}
